<h3 id="s2-3">2.3 Transformation of velocity and acceleration between rotating frames</h3>

<p>Yahan ek chhota sa mathematical tool chahiye, jo poori classical mechanics mein kaam aata hai â€” <strong>operator relation</strong>:</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Key tool â€” Transport (rotating axes) theorem</p>
  <p>Kisi bhi vector <span class="m"><span class="vec">A</span></span> ke liye, inertial frame (I) aur rotating frame (R) mein time derivatives ka relation:</p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">
    <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">A</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">A</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">A</span>
    <span class="lbl">Operator identity: (d/dt)<sub>I</sub> = (d/dt)<sub>R</sub> + Ï‰ Ã—</span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Padhne ka tarika: "inertial frame mein change rate = rotating frame mein change rate + axes ke ghoomne se aaya extra term".</p>
</div>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” is identity ka proof (simple version)</p>
  <p>Rotating frame ke basis vectors <span class="m">Ã®, Äµ, kÌ‚</span> likho. Koi bhi vector <span class="m"><span class="vec">A</span> = Aâ‚Ã® + Aâ‚‚Äµ + Aâ‚ƒkÌ‚</span>. Inertial frame se derivative lo:</p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0"><span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">A</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub> = (È¦â‚Ã® + È¦â‚‚Äµ + È¦â‚ƒkÌ‚) + (Aâ‚ dÃ®/dt + Aâ‚‚ dÄµ/dt + Aâ‚ƒ dkÌ‚/dt)</div>
  <p>Pehla bracket = <span class="m">(d<span class="vec">A</span>/dt)<sub>R</sub></span> (rotating frame ke andar change).</p>
  <p>Ab key step: <strong>rotating frame ke basis vectors khud <span class="m">Ï‰</span> se ghoomte hain</strong>, isliye <span class="m">dÃ®/dt = <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— Ã®</span>, aur wahi <span class="m">Äµ, kÌ‚</span> ke liye. (Ye intuitively sahi hai: spinaxis ke around ghoomti unit vector ki velocity <span class="m">Ï‰ Ã— r</span> hoti hai.)</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">To doosra bracket = <span class="m">Aâ‚(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— Ã®) + Aâ‚‚(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— Äµ) + Aâ‚ƒ(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— kÌ‚) = <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">A</span></span>. Bas, identity proved âœ”</p>
</div>

<h4>(i) Position / displacement</h4>
<p>Agar dono frames ka origin same ho (pure rotation), to position vector ka transformation sirf rotation matrix se hota hai (Section 2.2). Displacement ki <em>length</em> same rehti hai:</p>
<div class="eq">|<span class="vec">r</span>|<sub>I</sub> = |<span class="vec">r</span>|<sub>R</sub> = r</div>
<p>Sarva-origin coincident ho to <span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">r</span><sub>R</sub></span> (components alag, vector ek hi).</p>

<h4>(ii) Velocity transformation</h4>
<p>Transport theorem ko <span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span></span> par lagao:</p>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li><span class="m"><span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">r</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">r</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span></span></li>
  <li>Pehchaan: <span class="m">(d<span class="vec">r</span>/dt)<sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>I</sub></span> (absolute velocity) aur <span class="m">(d<span class="vec">r</span>/dt)<sub>R</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub></span> (frame ke andar maapi velocity).</li>
</ul>
<div class="eq">
  <span class="vec">v</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>
  <span class="lbl">Velocity transformation â€” rotating frame</span>
</div>
<p>Doosra term <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span></span> ko <strong>transport (entrainment) velocity</strong> kehte hain â€” ye sirf frame ke ghoomne se milti hai. Agar frame ghoomna band kar de (<span class="m">Ï‰ = 0</span>), to wahi purana result: <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub></span>.</p>

<h4>(iii) Acceleration transformation (poora derivation)</h4>
<p>Ye syllabus ka sabse important derivation hai is chapter mein. Dhyaan se, step-by-step:</p>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li>Equation: <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span></span>
    <span class="whyline">Ye humne abhi derive kiya.</span></li>
  <li>Ab inertial frame se derivative lo: <span class="m"><span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> = (<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub>)(<span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>)</span>
    <span class="whyline">Definition: acceleration = velocity ka inertial derivative.</span></li>
  <li>Dono terms par transport theorem lagao. Pehli term: <span class="m">(<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub>)<span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> = (<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub>)<span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> = <span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub></span>
    <span class="whyline">Yahan <span class="m"><span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub></span> = relative acceleration (frame ke andar maapi gayi).</span></li>
  <li>Doosri term: <span class="m">(<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>I</sub>)(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) = (<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub>)(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— (<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>)</span>
    <span class="whyline">Aur <span class="m">(<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub>)(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) = <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span><span>dt</span></span><sub>R</sub> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub></span> (product rule). Dhyaan do: body-frame mein <span class="m">d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>/dt</span> aur inertial frame mein <span class="m">d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>/dt</span> same hote hain kyunki <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> = 0</span>.</span></li>
  <li>Sab jod ke <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub></span> wala term <strong>do baar</strong> aata hai. Isliye coefficient 2:
    <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0"><span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> + 2<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— (<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) + <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span><span>dt</span></span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span></div>
    <span class="whyline">Term-by-term naam: (1) relative acceleration, (2) <strong>Coriolis</strong> acceleration, (3) <strong>centripetal/centrifugal</strong> term, (4) <strong>Euler</strong> (transverse) term â€” jo tab aata hai jab <span class="m">Ï‰</span> ki magnitude badle.</span></li>
</ul>

<div class="eq">
  <span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> = <span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> âˆ’ 2<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> âˆ’ <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— (<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) âˆ’ <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span><span>dt</span></span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>
  <span class="lbl">Rotating frame mein acceleration (inertial terms ko right side bhej diya)</span>
</div>

<h3 id="s2-4">2.4 Forces in a rotating frame â€” Coriolis force</h3>

<p>Ab dono taraf <span class="m">m</span> se multiply karo, aur <span class="m">m<span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">F</span><sub>real</sub></span> (inertial frame mein Newton's law valid hai) use karo:</p>
<div class="eq">
m<span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> = <span class="vec">F</span><sub>real</sub> âˆ’ 2m<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> âˆ’ m<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— (<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) âˆ’ m<span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span><span>dt</span></span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>
</div>

