<p>Earth ke liye <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span> constant hai (practically), isliye <strong>Euler force zero</strong>. Baaki do â€” centrifugal aur Coriolis â€” hi hamare daily life mein dikhte hain.</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Coriolis force (exam-ready)</p>
  <p><strong>In a frame rotating with constant angular velocity <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span>, a particle moving with velocity <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span></span> relative to that frame experiences a pseudo force <span class="m"><span class="vec">F</span><sub>cor</sub> = âˆ’2m(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span>)</span>, called the Coriolis force. Its magnitude is <span class="m">2mÏ‰v sinÏ†</span> and it acts perpendicular both to the axis of rotation and to the velocity of the particle. It does no work.</strong></p>
</div>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” Coriolis force ki 5 khaas properties</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Velocity ke perpendicular</strong> hai (kyunki cross product hai). Isliye ye path ko <em>mothi</em> ( deflect ) to hai, <strong>speed nahi badalti</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Work zero:</strong> <span class="m">W = <span class="vec">F</span>Â·<span class="vec">v</span> = âˆ’2m(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span>)Â·<span class="vec">v</span> = 0</span>, kyunki <span class="m">(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span>)</span> âŸ‚ <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span></span>. (Isi liye Coriolis force se kinetic energy nahi badalti.)</li>
    <li><strong>Velocity ke sign se ulti bhi ho jaati hai:</strong> direction <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span></span> ke saath flip ho jaati hai â€” jaise vertical upar jaate object par deflection west, neeche girte object par east.</li>
