    <li><strong>Mass ke proportional:</strong> halki cheez par kam, bhaari par zyada â€” lekin acceleration <span class="m">2Ï‰v sinÎ»</span> mass se independent! (Isliye pendulum ka plane ghoomta hai, chahe bob brass ka ho ya loha ka.)</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h3 id="s2-6">2.6 Motion relative to the Earth</h3>

<p>Ab hum apne favourite non-inertial frame â€” <strong>Earth</strong> â€” par ye theory apply karte hain. Earth <span class="m">Ï‰ = 2Ï€/86164 s rad/s â‰ˆ 7.29 Ã— 10â»âµ rad/s</span> se ghoomti hai (86164 s = <em>sidereal</em> din, kyunki rotation ko fixed stars ke relative maapte hain, Sun ke relative nahi). Chhota number lagta hai, lekin itne bade radius par asar dikhta hai.</p>

<h4>(1) Effective gravity (centrifugal effect)</h4>
<p>Earth par baithhe humare liye do "forces" ka combination feel hota hai: real gravitational force <span class="m">m<span class="vec">g</span></span> (centre ki taraf) aur centrifugal pseudo force <span class="m">mÏ‰Â²Ï</span> (axis se bahar ki taraf). Resultant acceleration ko <strong>effective acceleration due to gravity</strong> kehte hain:</p>
