<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” Coriolis ke real-world proofs</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Trade winds:</strong> subtropical high pressure se air equator ki taraf chalti hai; N hemisphere mein right deflect hokar <strong>northeast trades</strong> bante hain, S hemisphere mein <strong>southeast trades</strong>. Historical naam isi deflection se aaye.</li>
    <li><strong>River banks:</strong> N hemisphere mein rivers ka right bank (jaise flow ki direction mein dayan) zyada erode hota hai (e.g., studies of Siberian and other N-hemisphere rivers). Ye ek subtle effect hai, sirf Coriolis se nahi, meander geometry se bhi.</li>
    <li><strong>Railway tracks</strong> long distances par right rail zyada ghis jaati hai â€” iska measurement multiple studies mein report hua hai, lekin effect bahut chhota hai.</li>
    <li><strong>Cyclones:</strong> Bay of Bengal aur Arabian Sea ke cyclones (N hemisphere) anticlockwise ghoomte hain; Australia ke cyclones clockwise.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h3 id="s2-8">2.8 Foucault's pendulum â€” Earth ki rotation ka direct proof</h3>

<p>Ye syllabus ka sabse khoobsurat experiment hai. Sawal: <em>"Earth ghoom rahi hai â€” ye hum bina aasmaan dekhe, laboratory ke andar baithe kaise prove karein?"</em> 1851 mein LÃ©on Foucault ne jawab diya: ek lamba pendulum latka do. Uski swing ka plane <strong>dheere-dheere ghoomta dikhega</strong> â€” aur wo ghoomna sirf Earth ki rotation se aata hai.</p>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” physical idea (koi formula nahi, sirf soch)</p>
  <p>Pendulum ka swing plane inertial space mein <strong>fix</strong> rehta hai (kyunki us par koi horizontal force nahi lagta jo use modhe). Lekin <strong>ground uske neeche ghoomta rehta hai</strong>. To hum jo "plane ghoom gaya" dekhte hain, wo actually <em>hum</em> (aur zameen) ghhoom rahe hote hain. Jaise ek ghoomte carousel par baithhe aapko bahar ke khambhe ulti dishÄ mein ghoomte dikhte hain.</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Rotating frame ki language mein: pendulum bob ki velocity ke against <strong>Coriolis force</strong> lagta hai, jo uska plane systematically ek direction mein ghumata rehta hai.</p>
</div>

