</div>

<h4>(C) Inelastic collision aur coefficient of restitution</h4>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Coefficient of restitution</p>
  <p><strong>The coefficient of restitution <span class="m">e</span> is the ratio of the relative velocity of separation to the relative velocity of approach along the line of impact:</strong></p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">e = <span class="frac"><span>vâ‚‚ âˆ’ vâ‚</span><span>uâ‚ âˆ’ uâ‚‚</span></span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(0 â‰¤ e â‰¤ 1)</div>
  <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:0"><span class="m">e = 1</span>: perfectly elastic. <span class="m">0 &lt; e &lt; 1</span>: partially inelastic (sach mein yahi hota hai â€” cricket ball <span class="m">e â‰ˆ 0.5</span>, superball <span class="m">e â‰ˆ 0.9</span>). <span class="m">e = 0</span>: perfectly inelastic (chipak jaate hain).</p>
</div>
<p>Energy loss (target rest par) ko <span class="m">e</span> ke terms mein likh sakte hain:</p>
<div class="eq">Î”K = Â½ <span class="frac"><span>mâ‚mâ‚‚</span><span>mâ‚+mâ‚‚</span></span> uâ‚Â²(1 âˆ’ eÂ²)</div>
<p>Check: <span class="m">e = 1</span> â†’ loss zero âœ“; <span class="m">e = 0</span> â†’ maximum loss <span class="m">Â½Î¼uâ‚Â²</span> âœ“. Yahi formula "bouncing ball experiment" mein <span class="m">e</span> measure karne ke liye bhi use hota hai: bounce ki height <span class="m">hâ€² = eÂ²h</span>.</p>

