<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” H (hydrogen) best moderator kyun hai?</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Sabse jyada energy loss per collision:</strong> jab <span class="m">M = m</span> ho, to <span class="m">Î± = 0</span> â€” yani neutron ek head-on collision mein <strong>poori energy</strong> de sakta hai (bilkul equal-mass case, jahan velocities exchange ho jaati hain).</li>
    <li><strong>Average loss bhi maximum:</strong> <span class="m">Î¾ = 1 + <span class="frac"><span>Î± ln Î±</span><span>1 âˆ’ Î±</span></span></span> â€” ye "average logarithmic energy decrement" hai. H ke liye <span class="m">Î¾ = 1</span>, carbon ke liye <span class="m">0.158</span>, lead ke liye <span class="m">0.0095</span>. Matlab lead mein neutron ko â‰ˆ1900 baar takrana padega!</li>
    <li><strong>Isliye</strong> reactors mein <strong>light water, heavy water ya graphite</strong> moderators use hote hain, lead bhaari hone ki wajah se nahi.</li>
    <li>Total collisions: <span class="m">n â‰ˆ <span class="frac"><span>ln(Eâ‚€/E<sub>final</sub>)</span><span>Î¾</span></span></span> = <span class="m">ln(1 MeV / 0.025 eV)/Î¾ = 18.2/Î¾</span>.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

