<h3 id="s4-8">4.8 Motion of a system with varying mass (rocket)</h3>

<p>Ab ek naya twist: agar system ka mass hi time ke saath badal raha ho (rocket mein fuel jal raha hai, ya raindrop mein paani jud raha hai), to <span class="m"><span class="vec">F</span> = m<span class="vec">a</span></span> seedha use nahi kar sakte, kyunki <span class="m">m</span> constant nahi hai.</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">General equation (variable mass)</p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">
    <span class="vec">F</span><sub>ext</sub> + <span class="vec">v</span><sub>rel</sub> <span class="frac"><span>dm</span><span>dt</span></span> = m <span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">v</span></span><span>dt</span></span>
    <span class="lbl">v<sub>rel</sub> = mass particles ki velocity relative to the body (rocket ke liye exhaust ki speed, peeche ki taraf)</span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Rocket ke liye <span class="m">dm/dt &lt; 0</span> (mass kam ho raha hai), aur <span class="m">âˆ’<span class="vec">v</span><sub>rel</sub>(dm/dt)</span> term ko <strong>thrust</strong> kehte hain.</p>
</div>

<h4>Derivation â€” from momentum conservation (rocket equation)</h4>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li>Time <span class="m">t</span> par: rocket ka mass <span class="m">m</span>, velocity <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span></span>. Momentum <span class="m">= m<span class="vec">v</span></span>.</li>
  <li>Time <span class="m">t + dt</span> par: rocket ka mass <span class="m">m + dm</span> (<span class="m">dm &lt; 0</span>) aur velocity <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span> + d<span class="vec">v</span></span>; eject hua mass <span class="m">(âˆ’dm)</span> velocity <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span> âˆ’ <span class="vec">u</span></span> ke saath (<span class="m"><span class="vec">u</span></span> = exhaust velocity <em>rocket ke relative</em>, peeche ki taraf).
    <span class="whyline">Ye "before/after" bookkeeping hai â€” momentum conservation ke liye sirf system ko sahi define karna hai (rocket + exhaust).</span></li>
  <li>Total momentum conserve karo (free space, <span class="m"><span class="vec">F</span><sub>ext</sub> = 0</span>):
    <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">m<span class="vec">v</span> = (m + dm)(<span class="vec">v</span> + d<span class="vec">v</span>) + (âˆ’dm)(<span class="vec">v</span> âˆ’ <span class="vec">u</span>)</div>
    <span class="whyline">Simplify karke <span class="m">m d<span class="vec">v</span> + <span class="vec">u</span> dm = 0</span> (kyunki <span class="m">dmÂ·d<span class="vec">v</span></span> second order ka chhota term drop ho jaata hai).</span></li>
  <li>Rearrange: <span class="m">d<span class="vec">v</span> = âˆ’<span class="vec">u</span> <span class="frac"><span>dm</span><span>m</span></span></span></li>
  <li>Integrate: <span class="m">Î”<span class="vec">v</span> = <span class="vec">u</span> ln(mâ‚€/m<sub>f</sub>)</span>
    <span class="whyline">Jahan <span class="m">mâ‚€ = initial mass</span> aur <span class="m">m<sub>f</sub> = final mass</span> (poora fuel jala dene ke baad).</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="eq">
