<h3 id="s4-9">4.9 Angular momentum â€” concept aur conservation</h3>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Angular momentum &amp; torque</p>
  <p><strong>Angular momentum of a particle about a point O: <span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span> = <span class="vec">r</span> Ã— <span class="vec">p</span> = <span class="vec">r</span> Ã— m<span class="vec">v</span></span>.</strong> Torque about the same point: <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï„</span> = <span class="vec">r</span> Ã— <span class="vec">F</span></span>. Units: <span class="m">L</span> â†’ kg mÂ²/s (or JÂ·s), <span class="m">Ï„</span> â†’ NÂ·m.</p>
</div>

<h4>Equation of motion for rotation: <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï„</span> = d<span class="vec">L</span>/dt</span></h4>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li><span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span> = Î£<sub>i</sub> <span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub> Ã— m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">v</span><sub>i</sub></span> (system ke saare particles ka sum)</li>
  <li>Derivative: <span class="m"><span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">L</span></span><span>dt</span></span> = Î£ (<span class="vec">v</span><sub>i</sub> Ã— m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">v</span><sub>i</sub>) + Î£ <span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub> Ã— m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">a</span><sub>i</sub></span>
    <span class="whyline">Pehla term zero hai â€” kyunki <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span> = 0</span> har particle ke liye âœ” (cross product ka apne aap se zero hona).</span></li>
  <li>Newton's second law: <span class="m">m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">a</span><sub>i</sub> = <span class="vec">F</span><sub>i</sub></span> â†’ <span class="m">d<span class="vec">L</span>/dt = Î£ <span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub> Ã— <span class="vec">F</span><sub>i</sub> = Î£ <span class="vec">Ï„</span><sub>i</sub></span></li>
  <li>Internal force pairs ka contribution cancel: <span class="m">(<span class="vec">r</span>â‚ âˆ’ <span class="vec">r</span>â‚‚) Ã— <span class="vec">F</span>â‚â‚‚ = 0</span>
    <span class="whyline">Kyunki internal forces particles ko jodne wali line ke along hote hain (strong form of Newton's third law), to cross product zero âœ“</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="eq">
<span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">L</span></span><span>dt</span></span> = <span class="vec">Ï„</span><sub>ext</sub> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;âŸ¹&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; agar <span class="vec">Ï„</span><sub>ext</sub> = 0 to <span class="vec">L</span> = constant
<span class="lbl">Angular momentum ka equation of motion + conservation law</span>
</div>

<h4>System ka angular momentum â€” do hisse</h4>
<p>CM ke baare mein likhne par <span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub> = <span class="vec">R</span> + <span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub>â€²</span> use karke (aur <span class="m">Î£m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub>â€² = 0</span>, <span class="m">Î£m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">v</span><sub>i</sub>â€² = 0</span> ki wajah se cross terms gayab ho jaate hain):</p>
<div class="eq">
<span class="vec">L</span> = M<span class="vec">R</span> Ã— <span class="vec">V</span><sub>cm</sub> &nbsp;+&nbsp; <span class="vec">L</span>â€²
<span class="lbl">Orbital (CM ke around) + Spin/internal angular momentum (CM ke baare mein)</span>
</div>
<p>Yehi separation Chapter 5 (rigid body) mein kaam aayega: rigid body ki <span class="m">Lâ€²</span> ko moment of inertia tensor se likhenge.</p>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why conservation itni important hai â€” examples</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Ice skater:</strong> haath andar karti hai â†’ <span class="m">I</span> kam â†’ <span class="m">Ï‰ = L/I</span> badh jaata hai â†’ tez spin. (Kyunkin <span class="m">L = IÏ‰</span> constant, aur koi external torque nahi.)</li>
    <li><strong>Planet orbit (Kepler's 2nd law):</strong> gravity ka torque Sun ke baare mein zero hai (<span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span> âˆ¥ <span class="vec">F</span></span>), isliye <span class="m">L</span> constant â†’ <span class="m">rÂ² <span class="frac"><span>dÎ¸</span><span>dt</span></span> = constant</span> â†’ area swept per unit time constant = equal areas in equal times. (Chapter 6 mein detail.)</li>
    <li><strong>Neutron stars:</strong> collapsing core ka radius 10âµ guna ghat jaata hai â†’ spin <span class="m">Ï‰</span> astronomically badh jaati hai (<em>millisecond pulsars</em>).</li>
    <li><strong>Earthâ€“Moon system:</strong> tidal friction Earth ki rotation energy ko Moon ke orbit mein transfer karti hai â†’ Earth ka din dheere-dheere lamba ho raha hai (â‰ˆ 1.7 ms per century, ancient eclipse records se verify hua).</li>
