<h3 id="s4-10">4.10 Charged particle scattering by a nucleus (Rutherford scattering)</h3>

<p>Ab hum collisions ka poora machinery ek famous experiment par lagate hain. 1909â€“1911 mein Geiger aur Marsden ne Rutherford ke kehne par <strong>Î±-particles</strong> (HeÂ²âº, charge <span class="m">+2e</span>) ki patli gold foil par barsaat ki. Observation: zyadatar Î± seedha nikal jaate the, lekin <strong>kuch bahut bade angles par bounce back</strong> ho jaate the. Rutherford ne kaha: "It was almost as incredible as if you fired a 15-inch shell at a piece of tissue paper and it came back and hit you."</p>

<p>Is observation ka explanation: atom ka poora <strong>positive charge ek chhote nucleus</strong> mein concentrated hai. Coulomb repulsion se aane wala Î± deflect hota hai, aur large-angle deflection tab hota hai jab wo nucleus ke bahut paas se guzre.</p>

<h4>Setup aur conservation laws</h4>
<p>Î±-particle (charge <span class="m">Zâ‚e</span>, mass <span class="m">m</span>, initial speed <span class="m">vâ‚€</span>) nucleus (charge <span class="m">Zâ‚‚e</span>, mass <span class="m">M â‰« m</span>, practically fixed) ki taraf <strong>impact parameter <span class="m">b</span></strong> se aa raha hai. Do conservation laws use karte hain:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Energy conservation:</strong> <span class="m">Â½mvâ‚€Â² = Â½mvÂ² + <span class="frac"><span>kZâ‚Zâ‚‚eÂ²</span><span>r</span></span></span> (jahan <span class="m">k = 1/4Ï€Îµâ‚€</span>)</li>
  <li><strong>Angular momentum conservation:</strong> Coulomb force central hai (<span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span></span> ke along), to torque zero â†’ <span class="m">L = mvâ‚€b = mrÂ²<span class="frac"><span>dÎ¸</span><span>dt</span></span></span> = constant. Yahi <span class="m">b</span> ko "fix" karta hai.</li>
</ol>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why central force hone se problem simple ho jaati hai</p>
  <p>Kyunki force sirf <span class="m">r</span> par depend karta hai (direction nahi), (i) motion ek hi <em>plane</em> mein rehta hai, (ii) angular momentum conserve hoti hai, aur (iii) orbit ek <strong>conic section</strong> ban jaati hai. Repulsive Coulomb ke liye wo <strong>hyperbola</strong> hoti hai (isliye particle aa ke wapas chala jaata hai, kabhi "band" nahi hota).</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Chapter 6 mein hum yehi "central force" theory detail mein karenge â€” yahan result use kar rahe hain.</p>
</div>

<h4>Key results (derivation outline)</h4>
<p>Orbit equation solve karne par (Binet's formula se ya geometry se) impact parameter aur scattering angle ka rishta milta hai:</p>
<div class="eq">
b = <span class="frac"><span>k Zâ‚Zâ‚‚ eÂ²</span><span>2E</span></span> cot <span class="frac"><span>Î¸</span><span>2</span></span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; where E = Â½mvâ‚€Â² (initial kinetic energy), k = 1/4Ï€Îµâ‚€
<span class="lbl">Impact parameter vs scattering angle (repulsive Coulomb)</span>
</div>
<p>Aur distance of closest approach (head-on, <span class="m">b = 0</span>) ke liye: <span class="m">r<sub>min</sub> = <span class="frac"><span>kZâ‚Zâ‚‚eÂ²</span><span>E</span></span></span> (energy conservation se).</p>

<h4>Cross-section aur Rutherford formula</h4>
<p>Experimentally hum ek <em>single</em> particle nahi, ek beam bhejte hain â€” isliye hum poochte hain: "kitne particles <span class="m">Î¸</span> angle par jaate hain?" Iska jawab <strong>differential cross-section</strong> deta hai:</p>
<div class="eq">
<span class="frac"><span>dÏƒ</span><span>dÎ©</span></span> = <span class="frac"><span>aÂ²</span><span>4 sinâ´(Î¸/2)</span></span> = ( <span class="frac"><span>k Zâ‚Zâ‚‚ eÂ²</span><span>4E</span></span> )Â² Â· <span class="frac"><span>1</span><span>sinâ´(Î¸/2)</span></span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(a = <span class="frac"><span>kZâ‚Zâ‚‚eÂ²</span><span>2E</span></span>)
<span class="lbl">Rutherford scattering formula â€” 1/sinâ´(Î¸/2) dependence famous hai</span>
</div>
<p>Derivation ka skeleton (ek line mein): geometry se <span class="m">b = a cot(Î¸/2)</span>; phir <span class="m"><span class="frac"><span>dÏƒ</span><span>dÎ©</span></span> = <span class="frac"><span>b</span><span>sin Î¸</span></span> |<span class="frac"><span>db</span><span>dÎ¸</span></span>|</span> lagane par <span class="m">1/sinâ´(Î¸/2)</span> aa jaata hai. Ye "annulus (ring) ka area Ã· solid angle" ka simple idea hai.</p>

