<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Moderator ke liye hydrogen best hai, phir bhi graphite/heavy water reactors mein kyun use hote hain?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Kyunki hydrogen ke saath ek problem hai: ordinary hydrogen absorption cross-section bada hota hai â€” wo neutron ko "kha" leta hai (forming deuterium), aur chain reaction ke liye zaroori neutron bachte nahi. Isliye many reactors mein <strong>graphite</strong> (absorption bahut kam, lekin 115 collisions chahiye) ya <strong>heavy water</strong> (<span class="m">Dâ‚‚O</span>, hydrogen jaisa achha slowing par absorption kam) use hota hai. Ye "moderating power vs absorption" trade-off nuclear engineering ka classic issue hai.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Scattering angle <span class="m">Î¸ â†’ 0</span> ke liye impact parameter kya hota hai? Aur cross-section kaunse angle par maximum hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m">Î¸ â†’ 0</span> ke liye <span class="m">cot(Î¸/2) â†’ âˆž</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">b â†’ âˆž</span>: matlab bahut door se guzarne wale Î± bilkul deflect nahi hote. Cross-section <span class="m">âˆ 1/sinâ´(Î¸/2)</span> â€” <strong>forward direction (Î¸ â†’ 0) par maximum</strong>, aur back-scattering (<span class="m">Î¸ â†’ 180Â°</span>) par minimum (par non-zero!). Isi liye experiment mein chhote angles par counting rate bahut zyada hota hai â€” aur ~1 in 8000 particles hi 90Â° se zyada deflect hota hai.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q3. Rutherford scattering mein angular momentum ka role kya hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Coulomb force central hai, isliye torque zero aur <span class="m">L = m vâ‚€ b</span> poore motion mein constant rehti hai. <span class="m">b</span> ko hi <span class="m">L</span> decide karta hai, aur <span class="m">L</span> ka conservation hi trajectory ko plane mein rakhkar orbit equation solve karne deta hai. Energy + angular momentum â€” ye do conservation laws hi poora scattering problem solve kar dete hain (ye CLO 9 ka core idea hai).</p></div>
</details>
</div>

