<h4>Derivation of the precession rate</h4>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li>Setup: symmetric top (spinning top), pivot <span class="m">O</span> par fixed, symmetry axis vertical se angle <span class="m">Î¸</span> par tilted. Spin angular velocity <span class="m">Ï‰</span> apni symmetry axis ke along (fast), mass <span class="m">M</span>, CM pivot se distance <span class="m">l</span> par.</li>
  <li>Torque: gravity <span class="m">M<span class="vec">g</span></span> CM par lagta hai â†’ torque magnitude <span class="m">Ï„ = Mgl sinÎ¸</span>, aur direction <strong>horizontal</strong> (axis ke perpendicular, "tilt plane" ke perpendicular).</li>
  <li>Angular momentum: fast spin ki wajah se <span class="m">L â‰ˆ IÏ‰</span>, symmetry axis ke along (nutation chhoti maan kar).</li>
  <li>Gyroscopic equation: <span class="m">d<span class="vec">L</span> = <span class="vec">Ï„</span>dt</span>
    <span class="whyline">Yani <span class="m">L</span> ka <em>ise</em> change nahi hota, sirf uska <strong>direction</strong> thoda mudta hai â€” torque ke direction mein.</span></li>
  <li>Time <span class="m">dt</span> mein axis <span class="m">dÏ†</span> angle se mudta hai; <span class="m">L</span> ki tip ka displacement <span class="m">|d<span class="vec">L</span>| = L sinÎ¸ Â· dÏ†</span></li>
  <li>Equate: <span class="m">Mgl sinÎ¸ Â· dt = L sinÎ¸ Â· dÏ†</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">dÏ†/dt = Mgl/L</span>
    <span class="whyline">Dono taraf ka <span class="m">sinÎ¸</span> cancel ho gaya â€” isliye (leading order mein) precession rate tilt angle par depend nahi karta!</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="eq">
Î©<sub>p</sub> = <span class="frac"><span>dÏ†</span><span>dt</span></span> = <span class="frac"><span>Mgl</span><span>L</span></span> â‰ˆ <span class="frac"><span>Mgl</span><span>IÏ‰</span></span>
<span class="lbl">Fast spinning top ki precession rate (gyroscope equation: Ï„ = Î© Ã— L)</span>
</div>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” is result ke 4 important consequences</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Zyada spin (<span class="m">Ï‰</span> bada) âŸ¹ precession dheemi.</strong> Isliye lattu tez ghumao â€” wo "sukoon se" khada dikhta hai, dheere dheere precess karta hai. Dheema ghumega to gir jaayega.</li>
    <li><strong>Tilt angle se independent (leading order mein):</strong> <span class="m">sinÎ¸</span> cancel ho jaata hai â€” yahi kyunki precession ko 19th century ke physicists ne "surprising" kaha.</li>
    <li><strong>Nutation:</strong> Asli motion mein <span class="m">Î¸</span> bhi thoda oscillate karta hai (nutation) â€” precession ke upar chhoti si "nodding" motion. Torque-free case mein nutation nahi hoti.</li>
    <li><strong>Direction:</strong> precession us direction mein hoti hai jis taraf <span class="m">Ï„</span> <span class="m">L</span> ko modta hai â€” gyroscope girti nahi, balki apni axis ko ghumati rehti hai. Isi trick se bicycle ke pahiye ko sirf ek string par sambhal ke rakh sakte hain!</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">Solved Example 3 â€” gyroscope ka calculation</p>
  <p>Ek top: <span class="m">I = 2Ã—10â»â´ kg mÂ²</span> (symmetry axis ke around), <span class="m">M = 0.2 kg</span>, CM pivot se <span class="m">l = 0.05 m</span>, spin <span class="m">Ï‰ = 300 rad/s</span>. Precession rate?</p>
  <p><span class="m">Î©<sub>p</sub> = Mgl/(IÏ‰) = (0.2 Ã— 9.8 Ã— 0.05)/(2Ã—10â»â´ Ã— 300) = 0.098/0.06 = 1.63 rad/s</span></p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Matlab precession period <span class="m">T = 2Ï€/1.63 â‰ˆ 3.9 s</span> â€” aankhon se clearly dikhta hai âœ“. Agar spin <span class="m">Ï‰</span> aadha kar do (<span class="m">150 rad/s</span>), to precession <strong>double</strong> ho jaayegi (<span class="m">3.3 rad/s</span>) â€” aur lattu jaldi girne lagega.</p>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” precession asli duniya mein</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Earth ki precession:</strong> Sun aur Moon ke torque se Earth ki rotation axis â‰ˆ 26,000 saal ke period se precess karti hai â€” isse "precession of the equinoxes" hota hai aur pole star badalta rehta hai (aaj Polaris, ~12,000 saal baad Vega).</li>
    <li><strong>Gyrocompass / INS:</strong> Aircraft aur ships ke navigation mein gyroscopes isliye use hote hain kyunki unki axis fixed direction maintain karti hai.</li>
    <li><strong>Rifle ki goli:</strong> Barrel ke andar spiral grooves (rifling) bullet ko spin dete hain. Spin ki wajah se air resistance bullet ko tumble nahi kar paata â€” gyroscopic stability. Yahi principle hai.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h3 id="s5-9">5.9 Recap aur exam corner â€” Chapter 5</h3>
<div class="box recap">
  <p class="bt">Quick Recap â€” Chapter 5</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li>Rigid body = fixed mutual distances; 6 DOF (3 translation + 3 rotation).</li>
    <li>Rotation ka equation: <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï„</span> = d<span class="vec">L</span>/dt</span>; fixed axis ke liye <span class="m">Ï„ = IÎ±</span>.</li>
    <li>Inertial coefficients: diagonal = moments of inertia (<span class="m">I<sub>xx</sub> = âˆ«Ï(yÂ²+zÂ²)dV</span>), off-diagonal = products of inertia (<span class="m">I<sub>xy</sub> = âˆ’âˆ«Ïxy dV</span>). Sab milkar tensor <span class="m"><span class="vec">ð•€</span></span>.</li>
    <li><span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span> = <span class="vec">ð•€</span><span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span> â€” generally <span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span> âˆ¦ <span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span>; <span class="m">L<sub>âŠ¥</sub> = Ï‰ sinÎ¸cosÎ¸(Iâ‚ âˆ’ Iâ‚‚)</span> (lamina), aur <span class="m">Ï„ = Ï‰ Ã— L</span> bearing par lagta hai.</li>
    <li><span class="m">K = Â½IÏ‰Â² = Â½<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>Â·<span class="vec">L</span></span>; principal axes mein <span class="m">K = Â½(Iâ‚Ï‰â‚Â² + Iâ‚‚Ï‰â‚‚Â² + Iâ‚ƒÏ‰â‚ƒÂ²)</span>.</li>
    <li>Principal axes: jahan <span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span> âˆ¥ <span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span>; symmetry axis hamesha principal axis hoti hai.</li>
    <li>Euler's equations: <span class="m">Iâ‚Ï‰Ì‡â‚ âˆ’ (Iâ‚‚âˆ’Iâ‚ƒ)Ï‰â‚‚Ï‰â‚ƒ = Ï„â‚</span> (cyclic). Free rotation: smallest aur largest <span class="m">I</span> ke around stable, middle ke around unstable.</li>
    <li>Spinning top: <span class="m">Î©<sub>p</sub> = Mgl/IÏ‰</span>; zyada spin âŸ¹ dheemi precession; gyroscope equation <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï„</span> = <span class="vec">Î©</span> Ã— <span class="vec">L</span></span>.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="box exam">
  <p class="bt">Exam corner â€” Chapter 5</p>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Inertial coefficients define kijiye. Moments aur products of inertia mein farq bataiye.</li>
    <li>Ek case dijiye jahan <span class="m"><span class="vec">L</span></span> aur <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span> parallel nahi hote. Kya iska koi practical consequence hai?</li>
    <li>Principal axes kya hain? Aur inki khaas baat kya hai?</li>
