<h3 id="s6-2">6.2 Two-body problem â†’ one-body problem (reduced mass ka jaadu)</h3>
<p>Asli duniya mein Sun bhi hilta hai (thoda). Do bodies (masses <span class="m">mâ‚, mâ‚‚</span>) ke mutual gravitational attraction ke liye:</p>
<ul class="deriv">
  <li>Relative vector: <span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span> = <span class="vec">r</span>â‚ âˆ’ <span class="vec">r</span>â‚‚</span> (yani do bodies ke beech ka vector)</li>
  <li>CM ka motion: <span class="m">M<span class="vec">R</span> = mâ‚<span class="vec">r</span>â‚ + mâ‚‚<span class="vec">r</span>â‚‚</span>; koi external force nahi hone par CM <strong>free</strong> (uniform velocity) chalti hai.</li>
  <li>Relative motion ka equation nikalta hai:
    <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">Î¼ <span class="frac"><span>dÂ²<span class="vec">r</span></span><span>dtÂ²</span></span> = <span class="vec">F</span>(r) <em>rÌ‚</em> &nbsp;&nbsp; with &nbsp; Î¼ = <span class="frac"><span>mâ‚mâ‚‚</span><span>mâ‚ + mâ‚‚</span></span></div>
    <span class="whyline">Bilkul wahi reduced mass jo Chapter 4 (collisions) mein aaya tha! Yahi mechanics ki khoobsurti hai: ek hi idea baar-baar kaam aata hai.</span></li>
</ul>
<p>Iska fayda: 2-body problem ek <strong>1-body problem</strong> ban jaata hai, jismein ek "reduced mass" particle centre of force ke around ghoomta hai. Sunâ€“Earth ke liye <span class="m">Î¼ â‰ˆ m<sub>Earth</sub></span> (kyunki Sun bahut bhaari hai) â€” isliye Earth practically Sun ke around ghoomti hai.</p>

<h3 id="s6-3">6.3 Effective potential aur energy diagram (Chapter 3 ka connection)</h3>
<p>Central force ke liye energy conservation plus angular momentum conservation mila kar ek kaam ka trick ban jaata hai:</p>
<div class="eq">
E = Â½má¹™Â² + <span class="frac"><span>LÂ²</span><span>2mrÂ²</span></span> + V(r) = Â½má¹™Â² + V<sub>eff</sub>(r)
<span class="lbl">V<sub>eff</sub>(r) = V(r) + LÂ²/(2mrÂ²) â€” "effective potential"</span>
</div>
<p>Yahan <span class="m">LÂ²/(2mrÂ²)</span> ko <strong>centrifugal barrier</strong> kehte hain. Ye ek radial-motion-only problem hai (1-D!), jise hum potential energy curve se padh sakte hain.</p>

