<section id="paper">
<h2 class="chapter"><span class="chnum">Exam kit 3</span>Practice Question Paper (full solutions ke saath)</h2>
<p class="small"><strong>Instructions:</strong> Pehle khud likhne ki koshish karo, phir "Answer dekho" par click karke check karo. Jo question galat jaaye, us section ka recap dobara padho.</p>

<h3>Section A â€” Short answer (2 marks each)</h3>
<div class="qa">
<p class="q">A1. Inertial aur non-inertial frame mein farq bataiye (ek-ek example ke saath).</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a">Inertial frame: zero acceleration wala frame jismein Newton's laws directly valid hain (e.g. ground, constant-velocity train). Non-inertial frame: accelerating ya rotating frame jismein pseudo force add karni padti hai (e.g. braking bus, rotating Earth jaise lambe experiments mein, merry-go-round). Test: free body ka acceleration zero hai? Inertial. Warna non-inertial.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A2. Galilean transformation likhiye aur ek assumption bataiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m">xâ€² = x âˆ’ Vt, yâ€² = y, zâ€² = z, tâ€² = t</span>. Assumptions: (i) relative velocity <span class="m">V</span> constant hai (dono inertial frames), (ii) time absolute hai (<span class="m">tâ€² = t</span>), (iii) axes parallel hain aur <span class="m">t = 0</span> par origins coincident the, (iv) <span class="m">V â‰ª c</span>.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A3. Coriolis force pseudo force kyun hai? Uski magnitude likhiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a">Kyunki ye kisi doosri body ki wajah se nahi aata; ye frame ki rotation (<span class="m">Ï‰</span>) ki wajah se aata hai, object ke mass ke proportional hai, aur iska koi third-law reaction pair nahi hai. Magnitude: <span class="m">F<sub>cor</sub> = 2mÏ‰v sinÏ†</span> (<span class="m">Ï†</span> = angle between <span class="m"><span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span> and <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span></span>). Horizontal motion par: <span class="m">2mÏ‰v sinÎ»</span>.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A4. Conservative force ki conditions likhiye aur do examples dijiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a">(i) Work path-independent, (ii) <span class="m">âˆ®FÂ·dr = 0</span> closed loop par, (iii) <span class="m">âˆ‡ Ã— F = 0</span>, (iv) potential energy exist karti hai (<span class="m">F = âˆ’dU/dx</span>), (v) mechanical energy conserved. Examples: gravity, spring force, Coulomb force.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A5. Centre of mass ki definition aur uska ek property likhiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m"><span class="vec">R</span> = (1/M)Î£m<sub>i</sub><span class="vec">r</span><sub>i</sub></span>. Property: <span class="m">M<span class="vec">A</span><sub>cm</sub> = <span class="vec">F</span><sub>ext</sub></span> â€” internal forces CM ke motion ko affect nahi karte, isliye CM ek single particle ki tarah behave karta hai.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A6. Reduced mass kya hai aur two-body problem mein iska role?</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m">Î¼ = mâ‚mâ‚‚/(mâ‚+mâ‚‚)</span>. Do-body relative motion ko ek single particle ki problem bana deta hai: <span class="m">Î¼<span class="vec">r</span>Ìˆ = <span class="vec">F</span>(r)<em>rÌ‚</em></span>, jahan <span class="m"><span class="vec">r</span> = <span class="vec">r</span>â‚ âˆ’ <span class="vec">r</span>â‚‚</span>. CM alag se free chalà¤¤à¤¾ hai. Ye collisions aur central-force dono mein use hota hai.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A7. Coefficient of restitution define kijiye aur perfectly inelastic collision ke liye value likhiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m">e = (separation speed)/(approach speed) = (vâ‚‚ âˆ’ vâ‚)/(uâ‚ âˆ’ uâ‚‚)</span>. Perfectly inelastic: <span class="m">e = 0</span> (dono bodies chipak jaati hain, common velocity = <span class="m">V<sub>cm</sub></span>). Elastic: <span class="m">e = 1</span>.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A8. Moderator ke liye halke nuclei kyun chahiye? Ek-line reason.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a">Elastic collision mein energy transfer fraction <span class="m">4mM/(m+M)Â²</span> hota hai, jo equal masses (<span class="m">M â‰ˆ m</span>) par maximum (=1) hota hai. Neutron ka mass light nuclei (H, D, C) ke qareeb hai, bhaari nuclei (Pb) ke nahi â€” isliye halke moderators kam collisions mein neutron ko slow kar dete hain.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A9. Kinetic energy of rotation ka expression likhiye aur ek body ka <span class="m">I</span> bataiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a"><span class="m">K = Â½IÏ‰Â²</span> (fixed axis). General: <span class="m">K = Â½<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>Â·<span class="vec">L</span> = Â½Î£I<sub>ij</sub>Ï‰<sub>i</sub>Ï‰<sub>j</sub></span>. Solid sphere apne diameter ke around: <span class="m">I = 2MRÂ²/5</span>; disc: <span class="m">MRÂ²/2</span>.</p></div></details>

<p class="q">A10. Kepler's second law likhiye aur uske peeche ka conservation law bataiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody"><p class="a">"Sun se planet ko jodne wali line equal times mein equal areas sweep karti hai" â€” i.e. areal velocity constant: <span class="m">dA/dt = L/2m = constant</span>. Peeche <strong>conservation of angular momentum</strong> hai, kyunki gravitational force central hai (<span class="m">Ï„ = 0</span>).</p></div></details>
</div>

<h3>Section B â€” Derivations (long answer)</h3>
<div class="qa">
<p class="q">B1. Rotating frame ke liye velocity aur acceleration ka transformation derive kijiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody">
<p class="a">Operator identity se shuru: kisi vector <span class="m">A</span> ke liye <span class="m">(dA/dt)<sub>I</sub> = (dA/dt)<sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">A</span></span> (ye rotating basis vectors <span class="m">dÃ®/dt = <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— Ã®</span> se aata hai).</p>
<p class="a"><strong>Velocity:</strong> <span class="m">A = <span class="vec">r</span></span> rakho: <span class="m"><span class="vec">v</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span></span>.</p>
<p class="a"><strong>Acceleration:</strong> isi result ka inertial derivative lo aur identity dobara lagao:
<span class="m"><span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> = (<span class="frac"><span>d</span><span>dt</span></span>)<sub>I</sub>(<span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>) = [<span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub>] + [(<span class="frac"><span>d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span></span><span>dt</span></span>) Ã— <span class="vec">r</span> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— (<span class="vec">Ï‰</span> Ã— <span class="vec">r</span>)]</span>,</p>
<p class="a">yani <span class="m"><span class="vec">a</span><sub>I</sub> = <span class="vec">a</span><sub>R</sub> + 2<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>Ã—<span class="vec">v</span><sub>R</sub> + <span class="vec">Ï‰</span>Ã—(<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>Ã—<span class="vec">r</span>) + (d<span class="vec">Ï‰</span>/dt)Ã—<span class="vec">r</span></span>. Last step: har term ko <span class="m">m</span> se multiply karke left side rakh do, to Coriolis, centrifugal aur Euler forces milte hain (with negative signs).</p>
</div></details>

<p class="q">B2. Foucault's pendulum ki theory derive kijiye aur precession period ka expression nikaliye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody">
<p class="a">Horizontal plane mein small oscillations: <span class="m">áº = âˆ’Ï‰â‚€Â²x + 2Ï‰<sub>z</sub>áº</span>, <span class="m">Ã¿ = âˆ’Ï‰â‚€Â²y âˆ’ 2Ï‰<sub>z</sub>áº‹</span>, jahan <span class="m">Ï‰â‚€ = âˆš(g/l)</span> aur <span class="m">Ï‰<sub>z</sub> = Ï‰ sinÎ»</span> (Earth ke <span class="m">Ï‰</span> ka local vertical component).</p>
<p class="a"><span class="m">Î¶ = x + iy</span> lekar dono ko jodo: <span class="m">Î¶Ìˆ + 2iÏ‰<sub>z</sub>Î¶Ì‡ + Ï‰â‚€Â²Î¶ = 0</span>. Iska solution <span class="m">Î¶ = e<sup>âˆ’iÏ‰<sub>z</sub>t</sup>(A e<sup>iÏ‰â‚€t</sup> + B e<sup>âˆ’iÏ‰â‚€t</sup>)</span> â€” envelope <span class="m">e<sup>âˆ’iÏ‰<sub>z</sub>t</sup></span> ka matlab swing plane <span class="m">Ï‰<sub>z</sub></span> rate se ghoomta hai.</p>
<p class="a">Isliye <span class="m">Î© = Ï‰ sinÎ»</span> aur <span class="m">T = 2Ï€/(Ï‰ sinÎ») = 23.934 h / sinÎ»</span>. N hemisphere mein upar se dekho to clockwise; equator par <span class="m">T = âˆž</span> (koi precession nahi); poles par <span class="m">T â‰ˆ 23.93 h</span>.</p>
</div></details>

<p class="q">B3. 1-D elastic collision ka general result derive kijiye (CM frame method).</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody">
<p class="a">CM velocity: <span class="m">V = (mâ‚uâ‚ + mâ‚‚uâ‚‚)/M</span>. CM frame mein initial velocities: <span class="m">uâ‚â€² = uâ‚ âˆ’ V = mâ‚‚(uâ‚âˆ’uâ‚‚)/M</span>, <span class="m">uâ‚‚â€² = uâ‚‚ âˆ’ V = âˆ’mâ‚(uâ‚âˆ’uâ‚‚)/M</span>. Elastic collision mein CM frame ke andar speed magnitude preserve rehti hai aur direction ulti hoti hai: <span class="m">vâ‚â€² = âˆ’uâ‚â€²</span>, <span class="m">vâ‚‚â€² = âˆ’uâ‚‚â€²</span>. Wapas lab frame: <span class="m">vâ‚ = V + vâ‚â€² = ((mâ‚âˆ’mâ‚‚)uâ‚ + 2mâ‚‚uâ‚‚)/M</span> aur <span class="m">vâ‚‚ = V + vâ‚‚â€² = ((mâ‚‚âˆ’mâ‚)uâ‚‚ + 2mâ‚uâ‚)/M</span>. Special cases: <span class="m">mâ‚ = mâ‚‚</span> âŸ¹ velocities exchange; <span class="m">mâ‚ â‰ª mâ‚‚</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">vâ‚ â‰ˆ âˆ’uâ‚</span> (bounce back).</p>
</div></details>

<p class="q">B4. Rocket equation derive kijiye.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Answer dekho</summary><div class="dbody">
<p class="a">Time <span class="m">t</span>: mass <span class="m">m</span>, velocity <span class="m">v</span>, momentum <span class="m">mv</span>. Time <span class="m">t+dt</span>: rocket <span class="m">(m + dm, v + dv)</span>, exhaust <span class="m">(âˆ’dm, v âˆ’ u)</span> (<span class="m">u</span> = exhaust speed relative to rocket). Momentum conservation (free space):
<span class="m">mv = (m+dm)(v+dv) + (âˆ’dm)(vâˆ’u)</span>. Second-order term drop karke: <span class="m">m dv + u dm = 0</span>. Integrate: <span class="m">âˆ«dv = âˆ’uâˆ«dm/m</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">Î”v = u ln(mâ‚€/m<sub>f</sub>) = v<sub>e</sub> ln(mâ‚€/m<sub>f</sub>)</span>. Thrust: <span class="m">T = âˆ’u(dm/dt) = v<sub>e</sub>(âˆ’dm/dt) &gt; 0</span>.</p>
</div></details>

