<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” Z<sub>eff</sub> itna important kyun hai?</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Kyunki Unit I ki <strong>har periodic property</strong> isi se explain hoti hai: size (kitna tight) â†’ IE (kitna mushkil se nikalta hai) â†’ EGE (kitni aasani se leta hai) â†’ electronegativity (kitna kheenchta hai). Sirf teen cheezein yaad rakho: <strong>(1) Z<sub>eff</sub> â†‘ = electron tightly held; (2) n â†‘ = electron door; (3) shielding â†‘ = Z<sub>eff</sub> â†“.</strong> Baaki sab isi se derive ho jaata hai.</p>
</div>

<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 1</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Slater's rules se N (Z = 7) ke 2p electron ka Z<sub>eff</sub> nikaliye.</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Config: 1sÂ² 2sÂ² 2pÂ³. Same group (2sÂ²2pÂ³ = 5 electrons, khud ko chhod ke 4): 4 Ã— 0.35 = 1.40. nâˆ’1 (1sÂ² = 2): 2 Ã— 0.85 = 1.70. S = 3.10 â†’ <strong>Z<sub>eff</sub> = 7 âˆ’ 3.10 = 3.90</strong>.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Z<sub>eff</sub> kabhi Z ke barabar ho sakta hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Sirf <strong>hydrogen (aur Heâº, LiÂ²âº jaise one-electron systems)</strong> mein â€” kyunki wahan screen karne wala koi doosra electron hi nahi (S = 0, to Z<sub>eff</sub> = Z). Multi-electron atoms mein hamesha Z<sub>eff</sub> &lt; Z. (Isi liye H ka IE kisi bhi alkali metal se bahut zyada hai â€” 1312 vs 496 kJ/mol.)</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q3. K (Z = 19) mein 4s aur 3d mein se kaun pehle bharta hai aur Z<sub>eff</sub> se iska kya lena-dena?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">4s pehle bharta hai (<span class="m">[Ar]4sÂ¹</span>). Reason: 3d ke liye Z<sub>eff</sub> bahut zyada hota hai (kareeb 8â€“9) lekin 3d orbital <strong>nucleus ke bahut paas concentrated</strong> nahi hota; 4s orbital penetrates theek se nucleus ke paas (radial nodes ki wajah se) aur effectively kam energy rakhta hai. Yahan Z<sub>eff</sub> ka role hai â€” penetration ke saath mil ke 4s ko 3d se pehle fill karwaata hai (jise "n + l rule" bhi kehte hain: 4s ka n+l = 4, 3d ka n+l = 5).</p></div>
</details>
