<div class="box recap">
  <p class="bt">Quick Recap â€” Chapter 1</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li>Periodic property = atomic number ke saath regular repeat (electronic configuration ki wajah se).</li>
    <li><span class="m">Z<sub>eff</sub> = Z âˆ’ S</span>; screening/shirlding inner electrons ke repulsion se hoti hai.</li>
    <li>Screening power: f &gt; d &gt; p &gt; s; penetration order ulta: s &gt; p &gt; d &gt; f.</li>
    <li>Slater: 0.35 (same group) Â· 0.85 (nâˆ’1, s/p ke liye) Â· 1.00 (andar); nd/nf ke liye left ke saare 1.00.</li>
    <li>Standard values: Na 3s = 2.20, K 4s = 2.20, Cl 3p = 6.10, N 2p = 3.90, Zn 3d = 8.85.</li>
    <li>Period mein Z<sub>eff</sub> â†‘ (per step ~0.65), group mein ~constant â€” isliye size group mein badhta hai aur period mein ghatta hai.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="box exam">
  <p class="bt">Exam corner â€” Chapter 1</p>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> (i) Effective nuclear charge define kijiye. (ii) Shielding effect aur penetration mein farq bataiye. (iii) Slater's rules likhiye.</p>
  <p><strong>Long answer / numericals:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Slater's rules likhiye aur inka upyog karke Na, K, Cl aur Zn ke liye outermost electron ka Z<sub>eff</sub> nikaaliye. Har step explain kijiye.</li>
