<h3 id="s2-2">2.2 Covalent radii â€” octahedral aur tetrahedral</h3>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Covalent radius</p>
  <p><strong>The covalent radius of an atom is one-half of the internuclear distance between two identical atoms joined by a single covalent bond (Aâ€“A).</strong></p>
  <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:0">Clâ‚‚ bond length 1.98 Ã… â†’ Cl ka covalent radius 0.99 Ã…. Hâ€“H 0.74 Ã… â†’ H ka covalent radius 0.37 Ã….</p>
</div>

<p>Ab ek important baat: <strong>radius ka value coordination number (CN) par depend karta hai.</strong> Kyunki agar ek atom ke around zyada atoms bonded hain, to nucleus-electron cloud thoda "kheench" jaata hai aur bond lengths badh jaati hain. Isliye Pauling ne <strong>covalent radii ki do tables</strong> banayi:</p>

<div class="tw">
