<thead><tr><th>Scale</th><th>Reference (standard ion ka radius)</th><th>Naam</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>Goldschmidt</strong> (1926)</td><td><span class="m">r(Fâ») = 1.33 Ã…</span>, <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.32 Ã…</span> (CN = 6). Ye values crystal-structure data se nikali gayi (Wasastjerna ke molar refraction approach se).</td><td>Goldschmidt <strong>crystal radii</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Pauling</strong> (1927)</td><td>Theoretical method se <strong>univalent radii</strong> nikale (neeche formula), phir scaling factor se <strong>crystal radii</strong> banaye â€” inmein <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.40 Ã…</span>.</td><td>Pauling <strong>crystal radii</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Shannon</strong> (1976, modern standard)</td><td>Shannon ne do sets diye: <em>effective ionic radii</em> (jismein <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.26 Ã…</span>) aur <em>crystal radii</em> (jismein <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.40 Ã…</span>) â€” dono ka farq har ion ke liye <strong>constant 0.14 Ã…</strong> hota hai.</td><td>Shannon "effective ionic radii" / "crystal radii"</td></tr>
</tbody>
