</div>

<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” "ionic radii" vs "crystal radii": sabse bada confusion</p>
  <p>Syllabus mein "Ionic and crystal radii" alag-alag likhe hain, isliye exam mein ye farq poochha ja sakta hai. Standard (Shannon) presentation:</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Ionic radius (effective ionic radius):</strong> oxide ion ko <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.26 Ã…</span> maankar banaayi gayi radii ka set.</li>
    <li><strong>Crystal radius:</strong> usi data ka doosra set jismein <span class="m">r(OÂ²â») = 1.40 Ã…</span> maana jaata hai. Isliye <strong>crystal radius = ionic radius + 0.14 Ã…</strong> (har ion ke liye same offset).</li>
    <li>Ratna: radius ka <em>trend</em> aur <em>comparison</em> dono sets mein same hota hai; sirf absolute values 0.14 Ã… se shift hoti hain. Isliye kaunsa scale use kiya â€” ye question mein likh dena achhi practice hai.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

