<h3 id="s2-4">2.4 Pauling's method for ionic radii (univalent radii) â€” with worked example</h3>

<p>Pauling ka idea: isoelectronic ions mein radius <strong>Z<sub>eff</sub></strong> ke inversely proportional hota hai. Isliye:</p>
<div class="eq">r = <span class="frac"><span>C</span><span>Z<sub>eff</sub></span></span> = <span class="frac"><span>C</span><span>Z âˆ’ Ïƒ</span></span></div>
<p>Isi ko use karke do unknowns wali problem solve ho jaati hai (jaise Chapter 1 mein Slater's rules se Ïƒ milta hai).</p>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">WorkedExample â€” NaF crystal se Fâ» ka radius (standard textbook problem)</p>
  <p><strong>Diya hai:</strong> NaF mein <span class="m">r(Naâº) + r(Fâ») = 230 pm</span>. Dono ions Ne-type (10 electrons) hain, aur Ne-type ions ke liye <span class="m">Ïƒ = 4.5</span> (uses screening constant).</p>
  <ul class="deriv">
    <li>Z<sub>eff</sub>(Naâº) = 11 âˆ’ 4.5 = 6.5; Z<sub>eff</sub>(Fâ») = 9 âˆ’ 4.5 = 4.5</li>
    <li>Pauling's equation se: <span class="m">r(Naâº) = C/6.5</span> aur <span class="m">r(Fâ») = C/4.5</span>
      <span class="whyline">Dono isoelectronic hain, isliye constant C same hai â€” yahi is method ki jaan hai.</span></li>
    <li>Jodo: <span class="m">C(1/6.5 + 1/4.5) = 230 pm</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">C(0.1538 + 0.2222) = 230</span> âŸ¹ <span class="m">C = 611.5 pm</span></li>
    <li>Ab: <span class="m">r(Fâ») = 611.5/4.5 = <strong>136 pm</strong></span> aur <span class="m">r(Naâº) = 611.5/6.5 = 94 pm</span>
      <span class="whyline">Ye experimental values (Fâ» â‰ˆ 133â€“136 pm, Naâº â‰ˆ 95â€“102 pm) se achhe se match karta hai âœ“</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Lesson:</strong> isoelectronic ions mein radius <em>Z<sub>eff</sub></em> ke ulta hota hai â€” isliye NÂ³â» &gt; OÂ²â» &gt; Fâ» &gt; Naâº &gt; MgÂ²âº &gt; AlÂ³âº (Figure 2.2).</p>
</div>

