<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” anomalies ka exact reason (yahi exam mein poochha jaata hai)</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Be &gt; B (aur Mg &gt; Al, Zn &gt; Ga):</strong> Be ka config 1sÂ²2sÂ² hai â€” <strong>fully filled 2s</strong>. B ka 2sÂ²2pÂ¹ hai. Filled subshell zyada stable hai, aur B mein 2p electron nikalna <em>asani se</em> hota hai kyunki 2p orbital 2s se thoda higher energy aur zyada shielded hai. Isliye IE: Be (899) &gt; B (801) âœ“</li>
    <li><strong>N &gt; O (aur P &gt; S):</strong> N ka 2pÂ³ = <strong>half-filled</strong> (extra stability, exchange energy). O ka 2pâ´ hai â€” usme ek orbital mein <strong>do electron paired</strong> hain, jinki electron-electron repulsion energy badha deti hai, isliye ek electron hatana aasan ho jaata hai. Isliye IE: N (1402) &gt; O (1314) âœ“</li>
    <li><strong>Group 13 mein B &gt; Al, phir Ga &gt; In:</strong> B &gt; Al (size badhta hai, isliye IE girta hai), lekin Al ke baad Ga ka IE thoda <em>badh</em> jaata hai (d-block contraction ki wajah se Ga chhota ho gaya).</li>
    <li><strong>Transition series mein irregular:</strong> 3d electrons bharte waqt IE lagbhag flat rahata hai, kyunki Z<sub>eff</sub> badhta hai par shielding bhi badhti hai.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h3 id="s3-5">3.5 Applications of ionization enthalpy (syllabus mein explicitly likha hai)</h3>
<ol class="deriv">
  <li><strong>Metallic character aur reactivity:</strong> Kam IE wale elements aasaani se electron de dete hain â†’ metals. Isliye alkali metals sabse reactive metals hain (IE ~ 400â€“520 kJ/mol).</li>
  <li><strong>Oxidation states ka prediction:</strong> successive IE ke jumps se pata chalta hai kaunsi oxidation state stable hogi (Na: +1; Mg: +2; Al: +3).</li>
  <li><strong>Reducing power ka comparison:</strong> Kam IE = achha reducing agent. (Careful: aqueous solution mein hydration enthalpy bhi count karni padti hai â€” isliye Li paani mein Na se bhi strong reducing agent hai! Chapter 7.)</li>
  <li><strong>Bornâ€“Haber cycle se lattice enthalpy:</strong> Ionic compound banane ki energy accounting mein IE ek step hota hai.
    <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">Î”H<sub>f</sub> = Î”H<sub>sublimation</sub> + IE + Â½D + EGE + U<sub>lattice</sub></div>
    <span class="whyline">Example (NaCl): 108 + 496 + 122 + (âˆ’349) + (âˆ’788) = <strong>âˆ’411 kJ/mol</strong> â€” jo actual Î”H<sub>f</sub>(NaCl) = âˆ’411 kJ/mol se perfectly match karta hai âœ“</span></li>
  <li><strong>Bonding type predict karna:</strong> Kam IE + high EGE wale elements mein ionic bond banne ka chance zyada.</li>
  <li><strong>Group trends samajhna:</strong> S-block elements ki reactivity group mein neeche jaane par badhti hai (IE ghata hai), par water ke saath reaction ki vigour bhi badhti hai.</li>
  <li><strong>Inert pair effect:</strong> Bhaari p-block elements mein <span class="m">nsÂ²</span> electrons nikalne ki tendency kam ho jaati hai (IE s â†‘), isliye Tlâº, PbÂ²âº, BiÂ³âº stable hote hain â€” lower oxidation state stable (Ch 6 mein detail).</li>
</ol>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">Worked short question â€” IE se shell structure</p>
  <p><strong>Q:</strong> Ek element ke successive IE (kJ/mol) hain: 590, 1145, 4912, 6491. Iski likely oxidation state aur valence electrons?</p>
  <p><strong>Solution:</strong> I.E.â‚ = 590, I.E.â‚‚ = 1145 (dono ka ratio â‰ˆ 1.94 â€” normal). I.E.â‚ƒ = 4912 â†’ I.E.â‚‚ se <strong>4.3Ã— jump</strong>. Jump 2nd ke baad aa raha hai, matlab <strong>2 valence electrons</strong> hain. To element ek <strong>alkaline earth metal</strong> hai (actual values Ca ke hain), aur likely stable oxidation state <strong>+2</strong> hogi.</p>
  <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:0">Ye method "jump position se valence" ka classic exam question hai â€” pattern yaad rakho, values nahi.</p>
</div>

<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 3</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Noble gases ka IE sabse zyada kyun hota hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Kyunki unka config <strong>completely filled nsÂ²npâ¶</strong> hota hai â€” maximum stability. Saath hi Z<sub>eff</sub> us period mein sabse zyada hai aur size chhota. Isliye He (2372), Ne (2081), Ar (1521) sabse high IE rakhte hain.</p></div>
