<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. IEâ‚ aur IEâ‚‚ mein farq kyun hota hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">IEâ‚‚ ke waqt hum electron ek <strong>positive ion (Mâº)</strong> se nikal rahe hain. Do reasons: (i) ab ek extra proton jaisa effective charge hai (Z<sub>eff</sub> per electron zyada), (ii) wahi electron cloud ab ek kam electron ko hold kar raha hai â†’ electron-electron repulsion kam, nucleation stronger. Isliye hamesha I.E.â‚‚ &gt; I.E.â‚.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q3. Kya IE ko pehle measure karna aasan hai â€” solid se electron nikalna ya gaseous atom se?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Gaseous atom se. Isliye definition mein "isolated gaseous atom" likha hoga. Solid se nikalne ke liye pehle sublimation/atomization energy bhi lagti hai (jaise Na(s) â†’ Na(g) ke liye 108 kJ/mol) â€” wo alag quantity hai (sublimation enthalpy), IE nahi. Bornâ€“Haber cycle mein dono steps alag likhe jaate hain.</p></div>
</details>
</div>

<div class="box recap">
  <p class="bt">Quick Recap â€” Chapter 3</p>
