<h2 class="chapter"><span class="chnum">Chapter 4 Â· Unit I</span>Electron Gain Enthalpy &amp; Electron Affinity</h2>

<h3 id="s4-1">4.1 Definition â€” aur sign convention ki sabse badi trap</h3>

<p>Ulta process: atom <strong>electron le</strong> leta hai. Zyadatar atoms ke liye ismein energy <strong>nikalti</strong> hai (fayda hota hai), kyunki naya electron nucleus ki attraction se bandh jaata hai.</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Electron gain enthalpy (EGE)</p>
  <p><strong>Electron gain enthalpy is the enthalpy change when an isolated gaseous atom in its ground state accepts an electron to form a gaseous negative ion:</strong></p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">
    X(g) + eâ» âŸ¶ Xâ»(g) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Î”<sub>eg</sub>HÂ° = âˆ’ve for favourable cases (exothermic)
  </div>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Convention (yaad rakho):</strong> Cl ke liye <span class="m">Î”<sub>eg</sub>H = âˆ’349 kJ molâ»Â¹</span> â€” negative sign ka matlab <strong>energy nikli</strong> (favourable). Kuch textbooks isi ko "+349 kJ molâ»Â¹" likhkar "electron affinity" kehte hain.</p>
</div>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Electron affinity (EA)</p>
  <p><strong>Electron affinity is the amount of energy released when an isolated gaseous atom in its ground state accepts an electron to form a monovalent anion â€” i.e. it is the magnitude of the electron gain enthalpy for favourable cases (written as a positive number).</strong></p>
  <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:0">Rishta: <span class="m">EA = âˆ’Î”<sub>eg</sub>H</span> (jab process favourable ho). Cl: <span class="m">Î”<sub>eg</sub>H = âˆ’349 kJ/mol</span> aur <span class="m">EA = +349 kJ/mol</span> â€” dono <strong>same baat</strong> hai, sirf sign convention alag hai.</p>
</div>

<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” EGE vs EA (har saal marks katne wali galti)</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>EGE</strong> ek thermodynamic enthalpy change hai â€” sign ke saath likha jaata hai (âˆ’ve = favourable).</li>
    <li><strong>EA</strong> "kitni energy release hui" ka magnitude hai â€” isliye zyada EA = zyada stable anion = achha.</li>
    <li>Exam mein question jo term use kare, usi convention mein answer likho. Agar question "electron gain enthalpy of F is âˆ’328 kJ/mol" kehta hai, to "electron affinity of F is 328 kJ/mol" likhna correct hai.</li>
    <li>Be, N, Ne jaise elements ke liye EGE <strong>positive</strong> (unfavourable) ho jaata hai â€” aur unki "EA" likhna hi galat ho jayega (ya negative likhni padegi).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

