<h3 id="s4-3">4.3 Successive electron gain enthalpies</h3>
<p>Doosra electron jodhna mushkil hai â€” kyunki hum <strong>pehle se negative ion</strong> mein electron daal rahe hain (repulsion!). Isliye:</p>
<div class="eq">O(g) + eâ» â†’ Oâ»(g) &nbsp;&nbsp;Î”<sub>eg</sub>H = âˆ’141 kJ/mol &nbsp;&nbsp;(favourable)<br>
Oâ»(g) + eâ» â†’ OÂ²â»(g) &nbsp;&nbsp;Î”<sub>eg</sub>H = <strong>+780</strong> kJ/mol &nbsp;&nbsp;(unfavourable, endothermic)</div>
<p>To phir oxide (OÂ²â») ions wale ionic compounds bante kaise hain? Jawab: <strong>lattice energy ki wajah se</strong>. MgO mein <span class="m">OÂ²â»</span> ki second EGE (+780) lattice enthalpy se zyada se zyada compensate ho jaati hai (MgO ki lattice energy â‰ˆ âˆ’3795 kJ/mol), isliye overall compound banana favourable hai. Yahi Bornâ€“Haber cycle ka poora point hai.</p>

<h3 id="s4-4">4.4 EGE ke applications + syllabus link</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Bond type prediction:</strong> High (favourable) EGE + low IE â†’ ionic compound ka chance (NaCl).</li>
  <li><strong>Oxidising nature:</strong> Clâ‚‚/Fâ‚‚ jaise strong oxidisers. Dhyan: Fâ‚‚ ka EGE Cl se kam hone ke baawajood Fâ‚‚ strongest oxidiser hai â€” kyunki uska oxidising power <strong>Fâ€“F bond ki low bond dissociation enthalpy (158 kJ/mol vs Clâ‚‚ 243)</strong> aur Fâ» ki high hydration enthalpy se aata hai. Ye ek classic "trap" question hai â€” poora reasoning likhna.</li>
  <li><strong>Acidic/basic nature compare karna:</strong> Aanchal: badhate EGE wale elements ke hydrides acidic hote hain.</li>
  <li><strong>p-block periodicity ka "electron affinity" item</strong> (Unit I ka doosra paragraph) â€” ismein wahi concept hai jo yahan padhayaa gaya; trends group aur period dono mein same hain: period mein favourable â†’ group mein kam favourable (F anomaly ke saath).</li>
</ul>

<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 4</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Cl ka electron affinity F se zyada kyun hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">F atom ka size bahut chhota hai â€” uske 2p subshell mein naya electron daalte waqt strong inter-electronic repulsion hoti hai, jo released energy kam kar deti hai. Cl ka 3p subshell thoda bada hai, isliye repulsion kam aur EGE zyada favourable (âˆ’349 vs âˆ’328 kJ/mol).</p></div>
