<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” EN ke 4 common traps</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li>Electronegativity <strong>unit-less aur relative</strong> hai â€” "F ki EN 3.98 eV hai" likhna galat hai (3.98 Pauling units hai).</li>
    <li>EN <strong>isolated atom ki property nahi</strong> (contrary to IE/EA) â€” wo bond mein hi define hoti hai.</li>
    <li>Group mein EN <strong>ghatti</strong> hai (F 3.98 â†’ I 2.66) aur period mein <strong>badhti</strong> hai â€” par noble gases ke liye koi normal value nahi (He/Ne ki koi Pauling value nahi hoti).</li>
    <li>Hybridization badalne se EN badalti hai (sp &gt; spÂ² &gt; spÂ³) â€” isliye "carbon ki EN 2.55 hai" ek simplification hai.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” EN kaam kahan aati hai</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Bond polarity prediction:</strong> Î”X &gt; 1.7 â†’ mostly ionic (e.g., Naâ€“Cl Î”X = 2.23); 0.4â€“1.7 â†’ polar covalent (Hâ€“Cl 0.98); &lt; 0.4 â†’ non-polar covalent (Câ€“H 0.35).</li>
