<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” neeche jaane par catenation khatam kyun ho jaati hai?</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Do reasons: (i) <strong>Mâ€“M bond enthalpy ghatti hai</strong> (chhote size wale atoms ke orbitals achhe overlap karte hain; bade atoms mein overlap poori tarah se effective nahi hota), (ii) bade atoms ke around <strong>steric crowding</strong> badh jaati hai. Isliye silanes (Siâ‚™Hâ‚‚â‚™â‚Šâ‚‚) sirf kuch atoms tak hi bante hain (Siâ€“Si chain ~8 tak), Sn/Pb to metals ki tarah behave karte hain.</p>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” Sulphur aur boron bhi catenate karte hain</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Sulphur:</strong> Sâ‚ˆ rings (rhombic/monoclinic sulfur) aur polymeric chains (plastic sulfur) â€” ye bhi catenation hai (Sâ€“S bond ~266 kJ/mol).</li>
    <li><strong>Phosphorus:</strong> Pâ‚„ tetrahedron (white P), polymeric chains (red P).</li>
    <li><strong>Boron:</strong> boranes aur boron hydride cages (Ch 8) â€” boron "clusters" isi catenation ki advanced form hain.</li>
    <li><strong>Silicon:</strong> Siâ€“Oâ€“Si chains (silicones aur silicates) bhaari chains banate hain â€” par ye Siâ€“O catenation hai, Siâ€“Si catenation nahi (Ch 9).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 6</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Li aur Mg ki properties similar kyun hain? Do concrete examples do.</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Diagonal relationship: size/charge density aur EN ka net effect lagbhag same. Examples: (i) dono apne <strong>nitrides</strong> direct banaate hain (Liâ‚ƒN, Mgâ‚ƒNâ‚‚) â€” baaki alkali metals nahi; (ii) dono ke carbonates heat par oxide + COâ‚‚ dete hain; (iii) dono ke hydroxides weak bases hain aur dono organo-compounds mein covalent character dikhate hain (Mâ€“C bonds).</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Carbon catenation kar sakta hai par lead nahi â€” kyun?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Câ€“C bond enthalpy (347 kJ/mol) bahut high hai aur carbon chhota hone se orbital overlap excellent hai â€” chains stable. Neeche jaane par Mâ€“M bond enthalpy ghatti hai (Pbâ€“Pb â‰ˆ 150 kJ/mol), steric crowding badhti hai, aur metallic character badh jaati hai. Isliye silanes sirf chhoti chains tak bante hain aur Sn/Pb koi chain nahi dete.</p></div>
