  <summary>Q1. Paani mein Li sabse strong reducing agent hai (IE sabse zyada hone ke baawajood) â€” kyun?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Reducing power ka asli measure <strong>IE + sublimation + hydration enthalpy</strong> ka net (energy balance) hota hai. Li ka IE sabse zyada hai, lekin uska <strong>hydration enthalpy sabse zyada (âˆ’519 kJ/mol)</strong> hai (chhota ion) â€” aur ye IE ka extra hissa se zyada compensate karta hai. Net result: Li â†’ Liâº(aq) process sabse favourable â†’ Li paani mein sabse strong reducing agent. (Ise standard electrode potential se verify karte hain: EÂ°(Liâº/Li) = âˆ’3.04 V, jo sabse negative hai.)</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Ionic hydride mein hydrogen ka oxidation state kya hai, aur paani se reaction kyun itna tez hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Oxidation state <strong>âˆ’1 (Hâ» ion)</strong>. Reaction tez isliye hai kyunki Hâ» ek extremely strong base hai: <span class="m">Hâ» + Hâ‚‚O â†’ Hâ‚‚ + OHâ»</span> â€” proton transfer bahut exothermic hota hai (aur Hâ‚‚ gas nikalta hai). Isliye LiH/NaH/CaHâ‚‚ ko moisture se door rakhna padta hai.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q3. Crown ether Kâº ke liye selective kyun hai (Naâº ya Liâº ke liye nahi)?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Kyunki 18-crown-6 ka cavity diameter (~2.6â€“3.2 Ã…) Kâº ke size (r = 1.38 Ã…, diameter 2.76 Ã…) ke saath best fit karta hai â€” ion 6 oxygen atoms ke saath maximum number of favourable electrostatic contacts bana leta hai. Naâº chhota hai (fit dheela â†’ kam contacts) aur Liâº bahut chhota (15-crown-5 aur 12-crown-4 uske liye achhe hain). Ye "size-matched hostâ€“guest" chemistry ka classic example hai.</p></div>
</details>
</div>

