<h2 class="chapter"><span class="chnum">Chapter 8 Â· Unit II</span>Compounds of Boron â€” Diborane, Higher Boranes, Borazine &amp; Borohydrides</h2>

<p class="lead">Boron p-block ka sabse interesting element hai â€” kyunki uske paas <strong>3 valence electrons</strong> hain, to uske compounds mein "electron deficiency" hoti hai. Electron deficiency se hi wo ajeeb-geereeb structures bante hain: <strong>banana bonds, cage structures aur bridge bonds</strong>. Ye poora chapter isi "electron-deficient bonding" ki kahani hai.</p>

<h3 id="s8-1">8.1 Boron ke hydrides â€” overview</h3>
<p>Boron hydrogen ke saath bahut saare hydrides banata hai (boranes). Do families:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Series A:</strong> <span class="m">Bâ‚™Hâ‚™â‚Šâ‚„</span> â€” jaise Bâ‚‚Hâ‚†, Bâ‚…Hâ‚‰, Bâ‚†Hâ‚â‚€, Bâ‚â‚€Hâ‚â‚„ (ye "nido" boranes hain)</li>
  <li><strong>Series B:</strong> <span class="m">Bâ‚™Hâ‚™â‚Šâ‚†</span> â€” jaise Bâ‚„Hâ‚â‚€, Bâ‚…Hâ‚â‚, Bâ‚†Hâ‚â‚‚ (ye "arachno" boranes hain)</li>
</ul>
<p>Common names: <strong>Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† = diborane</strong> (sabse important), <strong>Bâ‚„Hâ‚â‚€ = tetraborane</strong>, <strong>Bâ‚…Hâ‚‰ = pentaborane</strong>, <strong>Bâ‚…Hâ‚â‚</strong>, <strong>Bâ‚†Hâ‚â‚€</strong>, <strong>Bâ‚â‚€Hâ‚â‚„ = decaborane</strong>, aur anion <span class="m">Bâ‚â‚‚Hâ‚â‚‚Â²â»</span> (closo).</p>

<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” "borane (BHâ‚ƒ)" khud nahi milta</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">BHâ‚ƒ ek electron-deficient species hai jo <strong>spontaneously dimerise</strong> hokar Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† ban jaata hai: <span class="m">2BHâ‚ƒ â†’ Bâ‚‚Hâ‚†</span>. Isliye simple "BHâ‚ƒ" gas as such stable nahi hota. Lekin BHâ‚ƒ ko ek Lewis base ke saath <strong>adduct</strong> ke roop mein stable kiya ja sakta hai â€” jaise <span class="m">Hâ‚ƒBÂ·NHâ‚ƒ</span> (ammonia-borane), <span class="m">Hâ‚ƒBÂ·CO</span> (borane carbonyl), <span class="m">Hâ‚ƒBÂ·O(Câ‚‚Hâ‚…)â‚‚</span> (boraneâ€“ether, jo THF/ether mein commercial solution ke roop mein milta hai). Ye boron ki Lewis acidity ka direct proof hai.</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s8-2">8.2 Diborane (Bâ‚‚Hâ‚†) â€” the star molecule</h3>

