<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” "symmetrical" aur "unsymmetrical" cleavage ko yaad rakhne ka trick</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Lewis base <strong>chhota aur strong</strong> ho (jaise NHâ‚ƒ) to diborane <em>asymmetric</em> tootata hai: ek BHâ‚ƒ do base leke cation banata hai [BHâ‚‚(NHâ‚ƒ)â‚‚]âº aur doosra BHâ‚ƒ hydride dekar anion [BHâ‚„]â» â€” ye "ionic" product hai.</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Lewis base <strong>bada/thoda kamzor</strong> ho (jaise ether) to diborane <em>symmetrically</em> tootata hai: dono boron atoms base ke saath neutral adduct banate hain (2Hâ‚ƒBÂ·ORâ‚‚). Simple yaad rakho: <em>NHâ‚ƒ = ionic products; ether = neutral adducts.</em></p>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” Diborane ka use aur safety</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Diborane ko reducing agent, rubber vulcanisation, aur boron-based materials (boron doping, boron nitride/boron carbide precursors) ke liye use karte hain. Lekin ye <strong>bahut toxic</strong> hai (TWA â‰ˆ 0.1 ppm) â€” 19th century ke researchers ko "boron hydride poisoning" bahut common maara karta tha. Isliye aaj ise sealed systems mein handle karte hain. History note: German chemist <strong>Alfred Stock</strong> ne 20th century ke shuruaat mein boranes par pathbreaking kaam kiya â€” aur unke banaye "vacuum-line" techniques aaj bhi inorganic chemistry labs mein use hote hain.</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s8-4">8.4 Higher boranes aur unka structure â€” closo / nido / arachno</h3>
<p>Higher boranes (Bâ‚„Hâ‚â‚€, Bâ‚…Hâ‚‰, Bâ‚â‚€Hâ‚â‚„, Bâ‚â‚‚Hâ‚â‚‚Â²â» â€¦) sab <strong>polyhedral cage</strong> structures banate hain, aur unki classification ek sabse khoobsurat rule se hoti hai â€” <strong>Wade's rules</strong> (skeletal electron pair counting).</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Wade's rules â€” simple counting (exam-friendly version)</p>
  <p>Ek borane <span class="m">Bâ‚™H<sub>n+m</sub></span> (charge <span class="m">q</span>) ke liye skeleton electron pairs nikaalo:</p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">
    skeletal electron pairs (SEP) = <span class="frac"><span>2n + m + q</span><span>2</span></span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Aur phir structure decide karo:</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>closo</strong> (closed polyhedron) agar SEP = <span class="m">n + 1</span> â€” e.g., <span class="m">Bâ‚â‚‚Hâ‚â‚‚Â²â»</span>: n = 12, m = 0, q = 2 â†’ SEP = (24+0+2)/2 = 13 = n+1 âœ“ closo</li>
    <li><strong>nido</strong> (nest-like, ek vertex missing) agar SEP = <span class="m">n + 2</span> â€” e.g., <span class="m">Bâ‚…Hâ‚‰</span>: (10+4)/2 = 7 = n+2 âœ“ nido; <span class="m">Bâ‚â‚€Hâ‚â‚„</span>: (20+4)/2 = 12 = n+2 âœ“ nido; aur <span class="m">Bâ‚‚Hâ‚†</span>: (4+4)/2 = 4 = n+2 âœ“ nido (isliye diborane bhi ek "nido" borane hai)</li>
    <li><strong>arachno</strong> (web-like, do vertex missing) agar SEP = <span class="m">n + 3</span> â€” e.g., <span class="m">Bâ‚„Hâ‚â‚€</span>: (8+6)/2 = 7 = n+3 âœ“ arachno</li>
  </ul>
</div>

