<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Borazine â€” preparation, structure, properties</p>
  <p><strong>Borazine (Bâ‚ƒNâ‚ƒHâ‚†) is a planar, hexagonal, six-membered ring of alternating boron and nitrogen atoms, each carrying one hydrogen; it is isoelectronic and isostructural with benzene, hence called "inorganic benzene".</strong></p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Preparation:</strong> <span class="m">3Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† + 6NHâ‚ƒ âŸ¶ 2Bâ‚ƒNâ‚ƒHâ‚† + 12Hâ‚‚</span> (diborane + ammonia, heat). Alternative: BClâ‚ƒ + NHâ‚„Cl se.</li>
    <li><strong>Structure:</strong> planar, D<sub>3h</sub>; 12 valence electrons ring mein (benzene ke jaise 6 Ï€-electrons); Bâ€“N bond length â‰ˆ 1.44 Ã….</li>
    <li><strong>Physical:</strong> colourless liquid, b.p. â‰ˆ 55 Â°C (benzene 80 Â°C se kam â€” weaker intermolecular forces); density benzene se kam.</li>
    <li><strong>Aromaticity (limited):</strong> Bâ€“N bond polar hone se ring mein electron delocalisation benzene se kam hoti hai. Isliye ye <strong>addition reactions</strong> (HCl, Brâ‚‚, Hâ‚‚O) aasaani se karta hai, jabki benzene substitution karta hai.
      <ul>
        <li>Hydrolysis: <span class="m">Bâ‚ƒNâ‚ƒHâ‚† + 9Hâ‚‚O âŸ¶ 3Hâ‚ƒBOâ‚ƒ + 3NHâ‚ƒ + 3Hâ‚‚</span></li>
        <li>Substitution with HCl/Brâ‚‚ at Bâ€“H bonds bhi possible (boron par electrophilic substitution-type behaviour)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Comparison with benzene:</strong> dipole moment â‰ˆ 0.5 D (benzene zero), ring polar, chemistry zyada reactive, thermal stability kam.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

