<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” BHâ‚„â» ki structure tetrahedral kyun hai?</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">BHâ‚„â» mein boron ke 4 bond pairs hain aur <strong>koi lone pair nahi</strong> â€” VSEPR ke hisaab se bond pairs maximum door rehte hain, yani <strong>tetrahedral (109.5Â°)</strong>. Iska electronic count bhi CHâ‚„ jaisa hai (8 electrons around B) â€” isliye "isoelectronic" kehte hain. Borohydrides ko VB theory mein bhi explain karte hain (B spÂ³ hybridisation) aur MO theory mein bhi (3câ€“2e-type delocalisation in Bâ€“Hâ€“M bridges when the cation coordinates).</p>
</div>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">Example â€” NaBHâ‚„ ka reducing action (organic chemistry ka link)</p>
  <p><span class="m">4Râ‚‚CO + NaBHâ‚„ âŸ¶ (in ethanol/water) âŸ¶ 4Râ‚‚CHOH + NaB(OH)â‚„</span> â€” yani carbonyl (C=O) reduce hokar alcohol ban jaata hai. NaBHâ‚„ ki khaas baat: ye <strong>aldehydes/ketones ko reduce karta hai par esters aur amides ko nahi</strong>. Isliye jahan selective reduction chahiye, wahan NaBHâ‚„; jahan strong reduction chahiye, wahan LiAlHâ‚„.</p>
