<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 8</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† mein bridge bonds ko "3câ€“2e" kyun kehte hain? Electron count karke dikhao.</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Kyunki ek bridge bond mein <strong>3 atoms</strong> (Bâ€“Hâ€“B) sirf <strong>2 electrons</strong> share karte hain â€” yani elecTrons "deficient" hain. Kula valence electrons: 2B Ã— 3 + 6H Ã— 1 = 12. Character terminal Bâ€“H bonds (4 Ã— 2 = 8 eâ») ke baad sirf 4 eâ» bachte hain, jo do bridge bonds mein lag jaate hain (2 eâ» per bridge). Isliye diborane electron-deficient hai aur Lewis acid ki tarah behave karta hai.</p></div>
</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Borazine ko benzene se compare karne par kaun-kaun se differences hain?</summary>
