</details>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q3. NaBHâ‚„ aur LiAlHâ‚„ mein se kaun strong reducing agent hai? Kyun?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a"><strong>LiAlHâ‚„</strong> â€” kyunki Alâ€“H bond zyada polar aur hydride (Hâ») transfer zyada easy hota hai; ye esters, carboxylic acids, amides tak reduce kar deta hai. NaBHâ‚„ milder hai, isliye selective reactions ke liye use hota hai (ketone/aldehyde reduce karega, ester ko chhodega). Ye "selectivity vs power" ka classic trade-off hai.</p></div>
</details>
</div>

<div class="box recap">
  <p class="bt">Quick Recap â€” Chapter 8</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li>Boranes electron-deficient hain; BHâ‚ƒ khud nahi rehta â€” dimer Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† banata hai ya adduct (Hâ‚ƒBÂ·NRâ‚ƒ, Hâ‚ƒBÂ·CO) deta hai.</li>
    <li>Diborane: 4 terminal 2câ€“2e bonds + 2 bridge <strong>3câ€“2e (banana)</strong> bonds; terminal Bâ€“H 1.19 Ã…, bridge 1.33 Ã…, BÂ·Â·Â·B 1.77 Ã….</li>
    <li>Preparations: 2NaBHâ‚„ + Iâ‚‚; 3NaBHâ‚„ + 4BFâ‚ƒ; 4BFâ‚ƒ + 3LiAlHâ‚„.</li>
    <li>Reactions: hydrolysis â†’ Hâ‚ƒBOâ‚ƒ + Hâ‚‚; NHâ‚ƒ (kam) â†’ unsymmetrical cleavage [BHâ‚‚(NHâ‚ƒ)â‚‚]âº[BHâ‚„]â»; NHâ‚ƒ (zyada/heat) â†’ borazine; ether â†’ symmetrical adduct; LiH â†’ LiBHâ‚„.</li>
    <li>Wade's rules: SEP = (2n + m + q)/2; closo n+1, nido n+2, arachno n+3. Examples: Bâ‚â‚‚Hâ‚â‚‚Â²â» closo, Bâ‚…Hâ‚‰/Bâ‚â‚€Hâ‚â‚„/Bâ‚‚Hâ‚† nido, Bâ‚„Hâ‚â‚€ arachno.</li>
    <li>Borazine "inorganic benzene": planar Bâ‚ƒNâ‚ƒ ring, Bâ€“N 1.44 Ã…, polar, addition reactions karta hai.</li>
    <li>Borohydrides: BHâ‚„â» tetrahedral; NaBHâ‚„ (mild, selective reducer, 10.6 wt % H), LiBHâ‚„ (18.5 wt % H); LiAlHâ‚„ strongest.</li>
  </ul>
