<h3 id="s9-1">9.1 Fullerenes</h3>
<p>1985 mein ek experiment ne carbon ki poori chemistry badal di. Scientists ne graphite ko laser se vaporise kiya aur mass spectrum mein ek strong peak dekha â€” <strong>Câ‚†â‚€</strong>. Matlab carbon ke 60 atoms milkar ek naya molecule bana rahe the.</p>

<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Fullerenes</p>
  <p><strong>Fullerenes are a class of allotropes of carbon consisting of closed cage-like molecules formed by carbon atoms arranged in pentagons and hexagons (a "buckyball" structure). The most famous is Câ‚†â‚€ (buckminsterfullerene), a truncated icosahedron.</strong></p>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">History (verified)</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Câ‚†â‚€ ki khoj <strong>1985</strong> mein <strong>H. W. Kroto, R. F. Curl aur R. E. Smalley</strong> ne ki (laser vaporisation of graphite se, aur mass spectrum mein Câ‚†â‚€ ka peak dekh kar). Namen <strong>Buckminster Fuller</strong> ke geodesic domes ke naam par "buckminsterfullerene" rakha gaya. In teenon ko <strong>1996 ka Chemistry Nobel Prize</strong> mila. Phir <strong>1990</strong> mein W. KrÃ¤tschmer aur D. Huffman ne arc-discharge method se <strong>gram-scale</strong> production kiya â€” isse fullerene chemistry tez aage badhi.</p>
</div>

