<h3 id="s9-2">9.2 Carbides</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Carbides</p>
  <p><strong>Carbides are binary compounds of carbon with a less electronegative element (metals or metalloids). They are classified by the nature of bonding into three types: ionic (saline), covalent and interstitial.</strong></p>
