<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” CFCs aur ozone: link zaroor likho</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">CFCs stratosphere mein UV light se decompose hote hain aur <strong>Cl atoms</strong> release karte hain, jo ozone (Oâ‚ƒ) ko catalytic cycle mein todte hain: <span class="m">Cl + Oâ‚ƒ â†’ ClO + Oâ‚‚</span>, phir <span class="m">ClO + O â†’ Cl + Oâ‚‚</span> â€” ek Cl atom hazaaron Oâ‚ƒ molecules tod sakta hai. Isliye <strong>Montreal Protocol (1987)</strong> mein CFCs ka production phase out kiya gaya. Ye chemistry ka syllabus-point nahi, par exam mein "fluorocarbons ke environmental effects" poochh liya jaaye to ye likhna chahiye.</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s9-4">9.4 Silicates â€” structural principle (syllabus ka important item)</h3>
<p>Silicon aur oxygen Earth ki crust ka ~75 % banate hain â€” aur inka basic building block ek <strong>SiOâ‚„ tetrahedron</strong> hai. Silicates ki poore structural chemistry ek hi sawal ka jawab hai: <strong>"tetrahedra kitne corners (oxygen) share kar rahe hain?"</strong></p>

