<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” Al substitution se zeolites itne useful ban jaate hain</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">SiOâ‚‚ ka framework neutral hai. Lekin agar kuch <strong>Siâ´âº ki jagah AlÂ³âº</strong> fit ho jaaye (aluminosilicate), to framework ko <strong>negative charge</strong> mil jaata hai, jise Naâº/Kâº/CaÂ²âº jaise cations balance karte hain. Isse do bade fayde hote hain: <strong>(1) ion exchange</strong> â€” paani ki hardness (CaÂ²âº, MgÂ²âº) hata kar Naâº dena (washing-powder zeolites), aur <strong>(2) molecular sieving aur catalysis</strong> â€” fixed pore size ke andar sirf usi size ke molecules ghus sakte hain (petroleum cracking, ZSM-5 catalyst). Yahi wajah hai ki zeolites industrial chemistry ke "sabse important inorganic materials" mein gine jaate hain.</p>
</div>

<div class="box quiz">
<p class="bt" style="color:#3a2f7a">Mini knowledge check 9</p>
<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q1. Câ‚†â‚€ ke baare mein: kitne pentagons, hexagons, atoms aur bonds?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a">Câ‚†â‚€ = 60 carbon atoms (vertices), 90 Câ€“C bonds (edges), <strong>12 pentagons + 20 hexagons</strong> (32 faces). Diameter â‰ˆ 0.7 nm. Har pentagon akela (isolated) hota hai â€” isi se cage stable banta hai (isolated pentagon rule).</p></div>
