<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Sâ‚„Nâ‚„ â€” structure, preparation aur properties</p>
  <p><strong>Tetrasulphur tetranitride (Sâ‚„Nâ‚„) is a binary sulphurâ€“nitrogen compound containing an eight-membered ring of alternating sulphur and nitrogen atoms, in an "extreme cradle" (Dâ‚‚áµˆ) conformation with a weak transannular SÂ·Â·Â·S interaction of â‰ˆ 2.586 Ã….</strong></p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Physical:</strong> gold-poppy coloured (orange-yellow) solid; explosive on heating/shock; insoluble in water, slightly soluble in organic solvents (benzene).</li>
    <li><strong>Preparation (classic):</strong> dry ammonia ko <span class="m">Sâ‚‚Clâ‚‚</span> (disulphur dichloride) ke <span class="m">CClâ‚„</span> solution mein pass karo: <span class="m">6Sâ‚‚Clâ‚‚ + 16NHâ‚ƒ âŸ¶ Sâ‚„Nâ‚„ + 12NHâ‚„Cl + Sâ‚ˆ</span> â€” ye standard textbook method hai (yields ke saath). Modern route: <span class="m">[(Meâ‚ƒSi)â‚‚N]â‚‚S</span> + <span class="m">SClâ‚‚/SOâ‚‚Clâ‚‚</span> se.</li>
    <li><strong>Chemical behaviour:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Paani/alkali se <strong>hydrolysis</strong>: ammonia, thiosulphate aur sulphite-type products deta hai (jaise <span class="m">Sâ‚„Nâ‚„ + 6OHâ» âŸ¶ ... + NHâ‚ƒ</span> type products). Textbook statement: "paani se dheere hydrolyse hokar NHâ‚ƒ aur sulphur-oxygen species deta hai".</li>
        <li><strong>Lewis base:</strong> proton (Hâº) accept karke <span class="m">[Sâ‚„Nâ‚„H]âº</span> banata hai (HBFâ‚„ ke saath) â€” N atoms par basicity.</li>
        <li><strong>Lewis acid</strong> bhi behave karta hai (sulphur atoms acceptor) â€” CuCl ke saath polymer banata hai.</li>
        <li><strong>Precursor</strong> hai (SN)â‚“ polymer (polythiazyl) ka â€” jo ek <strong>metallic conductor</strong> hai (aur low temperature par superconductor) â€” ye "non-metal se metal" ka famous example hai!</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Bonding:</strong> saare Sâ€“N bond lengths lagbhag same (~1.62 Ã…) hain, jo <strong>electron delocalisation</strong> dikhata hai; transannular SÂ·Â·Â·S interaction ko MO theory se explain karte hain (ye van der Waals sum se chhota par normal Sâ€“S bond se bada hai).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="box fact">
  <p class="bt">Did you know? â€” (SN)â‚“ polymer: pehla "metallic polymer"</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Sâ‚„Nâ‚„ ko heat karke polythiazyl <strong>(SN)â‚“</strong> banta hai â€” ek polymeric chain of alternating S and N. Ye 1975 mein pehla <strong>non-metal-based material</strong> tha jismein anisotropic metallic conductivity aur ~0.26 K par superconductivity observed hui (Nature mein publish hua â€” physics community mein sensation tha). Chemistry mein ye example dikhata hai ki "metal ka matlab metal element nahi, band structure hota hai".</p>
</div>

