<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” Fâ‚‚ ka bond Clâ‚‚ se kamzor kyun hai? (classic exam question)</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">F atom bahut chhota hai, aur Fâ‚‚ mein har F par 3 lone pairs hote hain jo ek doosre se <strong>repel</strong> karte hain. Ye repulsion Fâ€“F bond ko kamzor kar deti hai (158 kJ/mol), jabki Clâ‚‚ mein 3p orbitals bade hain (repulsion kam) to bond strong hai (243 kJ/mol). Isliye halogen bond enthalpies ka order: <strong>Clâ‚‚ &gt; Brâ‚‚ &gt; Fâ‚‚ &gt; Iâ‚‚</strong>. <em>Result:</em> Fâ‚‚ bahut reactive/strong oxidiser hai (weak bond + very high EN + strong Fâ» hydration), aur Clâ‚‚ bhi.</p>
