<h3 id="s10-3">10.3 Halogens ke chemical properties</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Oxidation states:</strong> F sirf <strong>âˆ’1 aur 0</strong> (kyunki F sabse electronegative hai, aur uske paas d-orbitals nahi hai). Cl, Br, I: <strong>âˆ’1, +1, +3, +5, +7</strong> (unfilled d-orbitals/promotion se). Dhyan: iodine mein +7 kam stable (inert pair effect + large size).</li>
  <li><strong>Diatomic molecules</strong> (Fâ‚‚, Clâ‚‚, Brâ‚‚, Iâ‚‚), non-polar, low m.p./b.p.; group mein size badhne se <strong>van der Waals forces badhti hain</strong> â†’ physical state gas â†’ liquid â†’ solid.</li>
  <li><strong>Reactivity:</strong> Fâ‚‚ &gt; Clâ‚‚ &gt; Brâ‚‚ &gt; Iâ‚‚ (oxidising power ka order; Fâ‚‚ sabse strong oxidiser). Iodine weakest â€” kai reactions mein wo reducers ban jaata hai (jaise Iâ‚‚ ko oxidise karna aasan: Iâ» â†’ Iâ‚‚ by mild oxidants).</li>
  <li><strong>Hydrogen ke saath:</strong> Hâ‚‚ + Xâ‚‚ â†’ 2HX. Reaction ki vigour Fâ‚‚ (explosive, cold dark) â†’ Clâ‚‚ (sunlight) â†’ Brâ‚‚ (heat) â†’ Iâ‚‚ (slow, reversible; HI decomposes). HX ki acidity: <strong>HF â‰ª HCl &lt; HBr &lt; HI</strong> (bond enthalpy ka order: Hâ€“F 568 &gt; Hâ€“Cl 431 &gt; Hâ€“Br 366 &gt; Hâ€“I 299 kJ/mol). HF weak acid hai kyunki Hâ€“F bond bahut strong + H-bonding.</li>
  <li><strong>Paani ke saath:</strong> Clâ‚‚/Brâ‚‚ paani mein ghul ke <strong>disproportionate</strong> hote hain: <span class="m">Clâ‚‚ + Hâ‚‚O â‡Œ HCl + HOCl</span> (isliye chlorine water bleaching/oxidising action deta hai). <strong>Fâ‚‚ paani ko oxidise</strong> kar deta hai (2Fâ‚‚ + 2Hâ‚‚O â†’ 4HF + Oâ‚‚) kyunki wo Oâ‚‚ se bhi strong oxidiser hai (electrolysis-type "Fâ‚‚ from aqueous HF" nahi hota). Alkali ke saath: <span class="m">2NaOH + Clâ‚‚ â†’ NaCl + NaOCl + Hâ‚‚O</span> (hypochlorite bleach).</li>
  <li><strong>Metals/non-metals ke saath:</strong> halides banate hain; Fâ‚‚ sabse energetic (many metals Fâ‚‚ mein jal jaate hain), Iâ‚‚ selective.</li>
  <li><strong>Anion formation:</strong> Xâ» ions; Fâ» sabse chhota aur hardest; Iâ» sabse bada aur easily polarisable (isliye covalent character zyada, jaise AlIâ‚ƒ covalent type).</li>
  <li><strong>Iodine ki khaas baatein:</strong> sublimation (solid â†’ vapour directly), starch ke saath <strong>blue-black colour</strong> (iodine test), aur Iâ‚‚ + Iâ» â†’ Iâ‚ƒâ» (triiodide, jo paani mein soluble hai â€” isliye KI ka use hota hai iodine ko dissolve karne ke liye).</li>
</ul>

<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” halogens ke 3 common traps</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>"Fâ‚‚ strongest oxidising agent hai kyunki uska EGE sabse zyada hai"</strong> â€” galat reasoning! F ka EGE Cl se kam hai. Fâ‚‚ ki oxidising power <strong>(i) weak Fâ€“F bond, (ii) high EN, (iii) Fâ» ki high hydration enthalpy</strong> se aati hai. Aise questions mein poora reasoning likho.</li>
    <li><strong>"Halogens sirf âˆ’1 dikhate hain"</strong> â€” F ke liye sahi, baaki ke liye nahi: Clâ‚‚O, ClOâ‚‚â», ClOâ‚ƒâ», ClOâ‚„â» mein Cl ke oxidation states +1, +3, +5, +7 hote hain.</li>
    <li><strong>HF weak acid kyun</strong> â€” ye "hydrogen bond" aur "Hâ€“F bond enthalpy" dono se explain hota hai; sirf "F electronegative hai" likhna adhoora hai (electronegativity to acidity badhati hai, kam karti nahi â€” yahan bond strength aur H-bonding dominate karti hain).</li>
