    <li><strong>ClFâ‚ƒ (AXâ‚ƒ):</strong> 3 bond pairs + 2 lone pairs â†’ spÂ³d, trigonal bipyramidal arrangement; lone pairs <strong>equatorial</strong> lete hain (kyunki 90Â° par 2 lone-pair repulsions se bachna hai) â†’ bache teen bonds ek line + do corners par â†’ <strong>T-shaped</strong> âœ“</li>
    <li><strong>BrFâ‚… (AXâ‚…):</strong> 5 bond pairs + 1 lone pair â†’ spÂ³dÂ², octahedral arrangement; lone pair kisi ek vertex par â†’ <strong>square pyramidal</strong> âœ“ (lone pair sabse peeche/base ke "upar" rehta hai).</li>
    <li><strong>IFâ‚‡ (AXâ‚‡):</strong> 7 bond pairs + 0 lone pairs â†’ spÂ³dÂ³, <strong>pentagonal bipyramidal</strong> âœ“ (5 equatorial + 2 axial) â€” aur yahan koi lone pair nahi hone se geometry distort nahi hoti.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

