  </ol>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Conceptual:</strong> ClFâ‚… kyun nahi banta par IFâ‚‡ banta hai? <span class="small">[Chlorine ka size itna bada nahi hota ki 5 F atoms comfortably accommodate kar sake aur uske paas adequate orbitals/energy na ho; iodine bada hai (size badhne se zyada atoms bind ho sakte hain) aur IFâ‚‡ experimentally stable hai. Iske alawa F ke saath bond banana ke liye halogen ka bada size favours higher coordination â€” isliye AXâ‚…/AXâ‚‡ sirf Br/I ke saath milte hain.]</span></p>
