  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>â‰ˆ 3.7 Ã— 10Â¹â° dps = 1 curie (Ci)</strong> â€” aur yahi 1 Ci ki official definition hai! Units: <strong>1 becquerel (Bq) = 1 dps</strong>; 1 Ci = 3.7 Ã— 10Â¹â° Bq; 1 rutherford = 10â¶ dps.</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s14-6">14.6 Radioactive equilibrium (short note)</h3>
<p>Jab ek radioactive series mein parent ki half-life bahut lambi ho aur daughter chhoti, to series mein ek <strong>secular equilibrium</strong> ban jaata hai â€” har member ki activity barabar ho jaati hai (parent ki activity se control hoti hai). Isliye natural uranium ke samples mein Â²Â³â¸U aur Â²Â²â¶Ra ki activity ratio constant rehta hai. Exam mein ye "principle of radioactive equilibrium" ke naam se aata hai.</p>

<h3 id="s14-7">14.7 Mass defect aur nuclear binding energy</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Mass defect &amp; binding energy</p>
  <p><strong>Mass defect (Î”m) is the difference between the sum of the masses of the individual nucleons (protons and neutrons) in a nucleus and the actual mass of that nucleus. The energy equivalent of this mass defect is the nuclear binding energy (B.E.) â€” the energy required to break the nucleus completely into its constituent nucleons.</strong></p>
  <div class="eq" style="margin:8px 0">
    Î”m = [Z m<sub>p</sub> + N m<sub>n</sub>] âˆ’ M<sub>nucleus</sub> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B.E. = Î”m Ã— cÂ² = Î”m (u) Ã— 931.5 MeV
    <span class="lbl">1 u = 931.5 MeV = 1.492 Ã— 10â»Â¹â° J (yahi conversion exam mein use hota hai)</span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Binding energy per nucleon = B.E./A</strong> â€” yahi nucleus ki stability ka real measure hai.</p>
</div>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">Worked Example 3 â€” helium nucleus ki binding energy (must-do)</p>
  <p><strong>Data:</strong> m<sub>p</sub> = 1.00728 u, m<sub>n</sub> = 1.00867 u, He-4 nucleus ka mass = 4.00151 u (atom ka mass 4.00260 u minus 2 electron masses â‰ˆ 0.00110 u).</p>
  <ul class="deriv">
    <li>Nucleons ka total mass: <span class="m">2(1.00728) + 2(1.00867) = 2.01456 + 2.01734 = 4.03190 u</span></li>
    <li>Mass defect: <span class="m">Î”m = 4.03190 âˆ’ 4.00151 = 0.03039 u</span></li>
    <li>B.E. = <span class="m">0.03039 Ã— 931.5 = <strong>28.3 MeV</strong></span></li>
    <li>B.E. per nucleon = <span class="m">28.3 / 4 = <strong>7.07 MeV/nucleon</strong></span> âœ“ (standard value)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Insight:</strong> 4 nucleons milkar ~28 MeV energy release karte hain jab He-4 banta hai â€” yahi fusion (stars, hydrogen bomb) ka energy source hai.</p>
</div>

