<h3 id="s14-8">14.8 Nuclear reactions aur Q-value</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Notation aur conservation laws</p>
  <p><strong>Nuclear reaction:</strong> <span class="m">áµƒX + áµ‡Y â†’ á¶œZ + áµˆW</span>, jise chhote roop mein <span class="m">áµƒX(b, d)á¶œZ</span> likhte hain (jaise Â¹â´N(Î±, p)Â¹â·O).</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Conservation laws (har nuclear reaction mein):</strong> (i) mass number A, (ii) charge/atomic number Z, (iii) total energy (mass-energy), (iv) momentum, (v) angular momentum aur (vi) baryon number (nucleons ki total ginti). <strong>Q-value:</strong> <span class="m">Q = (Î£m<sub>reactants</sub> âˆ’ Î£m<sub>products</sub>)cÂ²</span> â€” Q &gt; 0 matlab exothermic (energy release), Q &lt; 0 matlab endothermic (energy chahiye).</p>
</div>

<div class="box ex">
  <p class="bt">Worked Example 4 â€” Q-value calculation (Rutherford ki famous reaction)</p>
  <p><strong>Reaction:</strong> Â¹â´N(Î±, p)Â¹â·O. Masses: Â¹â´N = 14.003074 u, â´He = 4.002603 u, Â¹H = 1.007825 u, Â¹â·O = 16.999131 u.</p>
  <ul class="deriv">
    <li>Reactants: <span class="m">14.003074 + 4.002603 = 18.005677 u</span></li>
    <li>Products: <span class="m">1.007825 + 16.999131 = 18.006956 u</span></li>
    <li>Î”m = <span class="m">18.005677 âˆ’ 18.006956 = âˆ’0.001279 u</span> (products bhaari hain!)</li>
    <li>Q = <span class="m">âˆ’0.001279 Ã— 931.5 = <strong>âˆ’1.19 MeV</strong></span> â†’ <strong>endothermic</strong></li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Isliye is reaction ke liye Î±-particle ki energy kuch minimum (threshold â‰ˆ 1.3 MeV) honi chahiye. Rutherford ke paas RaC' ke Î± (â‰ˆ 7.7 MeV) the â€” isliye unka 1919 ka experiment (pehli <strong>artificial transmutation</strong>) kaam kar gaya âœ“. <strong>Lesson:</strong> Q negative hone ka matlab reaction "nahi hota" nahi â€” matlab threshold energy chahiye.</p>
</div>

