  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Ye ek hi reaction hai â€” par per-kilogram hisaab se fusion fission se bhi zyada energy deta hai (fusion â‰ˆ 3.4 Ã— 10Â¹â´ J/kg, fission â‰ˆ 8 Ã— 10Â¹Â³ J/kg). Iske alawa fuel (deuterium) samundar ke paani mein practically unlimited hai.</p>
</div>

<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” fusion itni mushkil kyun hai (aur sun mein hoti kaise hai)</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Do nuclei ko milane ke liye unhe ek doosre ke bahut paas laana padta hai â€” lekin dono positive hain, to <strong>Coulomb barrier</strong> cross karna padta hai. Iske liye ~10â¸ K (100 million K) temperature chahiye (jahan plasma banta hai aur nuclei enough kinetic energy paate hain). Sun ke core mein ye temperature ~1.5 Ã— 10â· K hai, lekin wahan <strong>quantum tunnelling</strong> aur bahut zyada pressure/density kaam karte hain, isliye fusion slow but steady hoti hai. Earth par: <strong>tokamak (magnetic confinement)</strong> aur <strong>laser inertial confinement</strong> â€” dono par research chal rahi hai (ITER project).</p>
  <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:0">Sun mein hydrogen fusion ka net: <span class="m">4Â¹H â†’ â´He + 2eâº + 2Î½ + 26.7 MeV</span> (protonâ€“proton chain ka net result).</p>
</div>

