<h3 id="s14-13">14.13 Atom bomb</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Atom bomb (fission bomb)</p>
  <p><strong>An atom bomb is an uncontrolled, supercritical nuclear fission chain reaction device in which fissile material (Â²Â³âµU or Â²Â³â¹Pu) is rapidly assembled in a supercritical mass so that the chain reaction multiplies exponentially within microseconds, releasing enormous energy (~10Â¹Â³â€“10Â¹â´ J, i.e. kilotons of TNT).</strong></p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Fissile material:</strong> Â²Â³âµU (enriched to &gt; 90 %) ya Â²Â³â¹Pu (reactor se). Critical mass approximate: Â²Â³âµU â‰ˆ 50 kg (bare), Â²Â³â¹Pu â‰ˆ 10 kg (bare) â€” reflector/compression se ye kam ho jaata hai.</li>
    <li><strong>Method:</strong> do subcritical masses ko jaldi milaana (gun-type) ya implosion (compression) se density badha kar critical mass ghataana.</li>
    <li><strong>Energy:</strong> ~200 MeV per fission; 1 kg Â²Â³âµU ke poore fission se theoretically ~8 Ã— 10Â¹Â³ J milte hain (â‰ˆ 20 kilotons TNT equivalent).</li>
    <li><strong>History:</strong> Manhattan Project (Los Alamos, R. Oppenheimer); 16 July 1945 ka Trinity test; Hiroshima (6 Aug 1945, uranium bomb) aur Nagasaki (9 Aug 1945, plutonium bomb).</li>
    <li><strong>Effects:</strong> blast wave, thermal radiation, prompt nuclear radiation, radioactive fallout (fission products), EMP; long-term health/environmental impact.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

