<h3 id="s1-4">1.4 Properties of relations â€” Unit I ki asli "alphabet"</h3>
<p>Ye paanch properties poori book mein baar-baar aayengi. Inhe <strong>digraph ke roop mein "dekhna"</strong> seekho â€” phir ratta nahi lagana padega.</p>
<div class="tw">
<table>
<caption>Relation ki properties â€” definition (set form + digraph form)</caption>
<thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Definition</th><th>Digraph/matrix mein pehchaan</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>Reflexive</strong></td><td>âˆ€ a âˆˆ A, (a, a) âˆˆ R</td><td>Har vertex par <strong>loop</strong> ho; matrix ki diagonal sab 1</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Irreflexive</strong></td><td>âˆ€ a âˆˆ A, (a, a) âˆ‰ R</td><td>Kisi vertex par loop nahi; diagonal sab 0</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Symmetric</strong></td><td>(a, b) âˆˆ R âŸ¹ (b, a) âˆˆ R</td><td>Har arrow ka <strong>ulta arrow bhi</strong> ho (do-tarfa arrows)</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Antisymmetric</strong></td><td>(a, b) âˆˆ R aur (b, a) âˆˆ R âŸ¹ a = b</td><td>Do alag vertices ke beech <strong>kabhi bhi dono taraf arrow nahi</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Transitive</strong></td><td>(a, b) âˆˆ R aur (b, c) âˆˆ R âŸ¹ (a, c) âˆˆ R</td><td>Do arrows se bani "chain" ka <strong>shortcut arrow</strong> bhi ho</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Asymmetric</strong></td><td>(a, b) âˆˆ R âŸ¹ (b, a) âˆ‰ R</td><td>Koi bhi do-tarfa jodi nahi (strict relations mein)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

