<h3 id="s3-3">3.3 Chains aur anti-chains</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definitions</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Chain (linearly ordered set / total order):</strong> Poset (A, â‰¼) ka subset C aisa ho ki C ke <em>har</em> do elements comparable hon. Yaani <span class="m">a, b âˆˆ C âŸ¹ a â‰¼ b ya b â‰¼ a</span>. (Poora poset agar chain ho to usko <strong>total order</strong> ya <strong>linear order</strong> kehte hain.)</li>
    <li><strong>Anti-chain:</strong> Subset A' aisa ho ki uske koi bhi do elements comparable <strong>na</strong> hon â€” yaani sab pairwise incomparable.</li>
    <li><strong>Height</strong> = sabse lambi chain ke elements ki ginti. &nbsp; <strong>Width</strong> = sabse badi anti-chain ka size.</li>
  </ul>
