<details class="quiz">
  <summary>Q2. Kya (â„¤âº, |) distributive hai? Kya complemented hai?</summary>
  <div class="dbody"><p class="a"><strong>Distributive:</strong> haan â€” sabse badi baat ye hai ki gcd aur lcm hamesha distribute karte hain: <span class="m">gcd(a, lcm(b,c)) = lcm(gcd(a,b), gcd(a,c))</span>. <strong>Complemented:</strong> nahi! Kyunki (â„¤âº, |) <em>bounded</em> hai? Least element 1 hai, par greatest element hi nahi (koi sabse bada integer nahi hota) â†’ bounded nahi â†’ complemented ka sawaal hi nahi. (Bounded hona complemented hone ki shart hai.)</p></div>
