<h3 id="s6-1">6.1 Boolean function â€” definition aur truth table</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Boolean function</p>
  <p><strong>A Boolean function of n variables is a function f : {0, 1}â¿ â†’ {0, 1} â€” yaani n boolean inputs (0/1) lekar ek boolean output (0/1) deti hai. Ise ek boolean expression se (AND, OR, NOT ke saath) likha ja sakta hai, aur poori tarah uske truth table se bhi.</strong></p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">n variables ke liye truth table mein <span class="m">2â¿</span> rows hoti hain, aur total Boolean functions <span class="m">2^(2â¿)</span> ban sakte hain: n = 2 ke liye 16 functions, n = 3 ke liye 256, n = 4 ke liye 65536.</p>
</div>
<p>Do functions <strong>equivalent</strong> kehlate hain agar unki truth tables bilkul same hon (yaani saare inputs par same output). Isliye truth table ek Boolean function ka "fingerprint" hai â€” aur chapter ka poora kaam hai: <em>function ki expression nikaalna</em> aur <em>usko chhota karna</em>.</p>

<h3 id="s6-2">6.2 Minterm aur maxterm â€” normal forms ki building blocks</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definitions (carefully padho â€” yahin 90% galtiyan hoti hain)</p>
  <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Minterm (máµ¢):</strong> n variables ka ek <em>product</em> (AND) jisme har variable exactly ek baar aaà¤¤à¤¾ hai â€” direct ya complemented form mein. Minterm row <span class="m">i</span> ke liye sirf us row par <strong>1</strong> hota hai.</li>
    <li><strong>Maxterm (Máµ¢):</strong> n variables ka ek <em>sum</em> (OR) jisme har variable exactly ek baar aata hai. Maxterm row <span class="m">i</span> ke liye sirf us row par <strong>0</strong> hota hai.</li>
    <li><strong>Rule yaad rakho:</strong> minterm mein variable <strong>0 ho to complemented</strong> (xâ€²) aur <strong>1 ho to direct</strong> (x). Maxterm mein <strong>ulta</strong>: variable 0 ho to direct (x) aur 1 ho to complemented (xâ€²).</li>
    <li>Aur <span class="m">Máµ¢ = máµ¢â€²</span> (maxterm, minterm ka complement hota hai).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

