<h3 id="s6-3">6.3 DNF (Disjunctive Normal Form / sum of products)</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” DNF / PDNF</p>
  <p><strong>DNF (sum of products): products (minterms ya general terms) ka OR. Agar usmein sirf minterms hon to use "principal / canonical DNF" ya "sum of minterms" kehte hain aur likhte hain</strong> <span class="m">f = Î£m(iâ‚, iâ‚‚, â€¦)</span>.</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Method (truth table se):</strong> truth table ki wo saari rows chuno jahan <span class="m">f = 1</span> ho; har row ka minterm likho; sabko OR kar do. Bas! (Isliye DNF hamesha "1 wali rows" se banta hai.)</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s6-4">6.4 CNF (Conjunctive Normal Form / product of sums)</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” CNF / PCNF</p>
  <p><strong>CNF (product of sums): sums (maxterms ya general sums) ka AND. Sirf maxterms wale form ko "principal / canonical CNF" ya "product of maxterms" kehte hain aur likhte hain</strong> <span class="m">f = Î M(jâ‚, jâ‚‚, â€¦)</span>.</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Method (truth table se):</strong> wo rows chuno jahan <span class="m">f = 0</span> ho; har row ka maxterm likho; sabko AND kar do. (Isliye CNF "0 wali rows" se banta hai.)</p>
