<h3 id="s6-5">6.5 Simplification aur complete sets of connectives</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Simplify kyun?</strong> Chhota expression = kam gates = sasta aur fast circuit. Simplification ke tools: boolean laws (idempotent, absorption, distributivity, De Morgan) aur <em>Karnaugh map (K-map)</em> â€” jo aap aage padhenge. Exam mein laws se simplification likhna hi kaafi hota hai.</li>
  <li><strong>Complete set of connectives:</strong> aisa set jinse baaki saare boolean expressions bana sakein â€” jaise <span class="m">{AND, OR, NOT}</span>. Aur <span class="m">{NAND}</span> akela, ya <span class="m">{NOR}</span> akela bhi complete hai ("universal gates") â€” isliye real chips mein NAND/NOR hi zyada use hote hain.</li>
  <li><strong>Kaunsa normal form chuno?</strong> Agar truth table mein <em>kam rows f = 1</em> hain to DNF chhota milega; agar <em>kam rows f = 0</em> hain to CNF chhota milega. Ye ek exam-trick hai â€” pehle ginti dekho, phir choose karo.</li>
</ul>

<div class="box warn">
  <p class="bt">Careful! â€” DNF/CNF ke traps</p>
  <ol style="margin-bottom:0">
    <li><strong>Minterm mein complement ulta hota hai:</strong> row x = 0, y = 1, z = 0 ke liye minterm <span class="m">xâ€²yzâ€²</span> hai â€” 1 wala variable direct, 0 wala complemented. Maxterm mein exact ulta. Yahi ek rule poore question ka score decide karta hai.</li>
    <li><strong>CNF ke liye 0 wali rows chahiye</strong> â€” kai students galti se CNF bhi 1 wali rows se bana dete hain (aur answer galat aata hai).</li>
    <li><strong>DNF aur CNF ka answer different dikh sakta hai</strong> â€” par dono <em>same function</em> dete hain. Verify karne ke liye 2â€“3 rows par dono ko test karo.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

