  <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>Conceptual:</strong> Kya DNF aur CNF ek hi function ke liye hamesha dono majood hote hain? <span class="small">[Haan â€” kyunki har function ki truth table hoti hai, aur uski 1-wali rows se DNF aur 0-wali rows se CNF banti hi hai. Haan, edge case: constant function f â‰¡ 1 ka DNF = 1 aur CNF = âˆ… (koi maxterm nahi); f â‰¡ 0 ka ulta. Isliye "har function ke dono forms hote hain" (kabhi-kabhi trivial).]</span></p>
