<h2 class="chapter"><span class="chnum">Chapter 10 Â· Unit II</span>Discrete Numeric Functions</h2>

<p class="lead">"Discrete numeric function" ek fancy naam hai ek simple cheez ka: <strong>ek sequence</strong> â€” aâ‚€, aâ‚, aâ‚‚, â€¦ jo sirf integer points par defined hai (continuous function nahi). Poora Unit II isi tarah ke functions par operations, unki growth, aur unko "generating function" mein badalne ka kaam karta hai.</p>

<h3 id="s10-1">10.1 Definition aur examples</h3>
<div class="box def">
  <p class="bt">Definition â€” Discrete numeric function</p>
  <p><strong>A function a : â„• â†’ â„ (ya â„¤) is called a discrete numeric function â€” yaani ek aisa function jo non-negative integers par define ho. Iske values ko ek sequence ki tarah likhte hain:</strong></p>
