<div class="box why">
  <p class="bt">Why â€” "p false ho to p â†’ q hamesha true" ka matlab kya hai?</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">Isse <strong>vacuous truth</strong> kehte hain. Socho: "agar aaj baarish hogi, to main chhata le jaunga." Agar baarish <em>hi nahi hui</em> (p false), to aapki baat ko jhoota kaun keh sakta hai? Aapne promise todÐ° nahi â€” isliye implication true mana jaata hai (chahe aap chhata le gaye ya nahi). Yahi convention maths ko consistent rakhta hai aur isi se <span class="m">p â†’ q â‰¡ Â¬p âˆ¨ q</span> banta hai â€” ye equivalence poore logic ki "jaan" hai.</p>
</div>

<h3 id="s9-2">9.2 Compound statements aur truth table banana</h3>
<p><strong>Steps:</strong> (1) saare variables ki rows likho (<span class="m">2â¿</span> rows, n variables); (2) chhote se bade sub-expressions ke columns banao; (3) andar se bahar compute karo; (4) last column main expression hoga.</p>
